From c108f6292a3d9ce969dac5145f6e35aa2634f8dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:55:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 036/547] Fix the duplicate min_playback_duration_description
 resource

:app:mergeCoreReleaseResources failed with "Found item
String/min_playback_duration_description more than one time", which stops the
build before the app module's Kotlin is compiled at all.

"Fix the stats charts" wanted the setting's summary to state the current
threshold, and added a parameterised string for it - but appended it rather
than replacing the plain one already in the file, so strings-ot.xml declared
the same name twice.

Replacing the original in place would have been the obvious fix and the wrong
one: twenty-odd translations define that name with no format placeholder, and
the dialog still uses it without an argument, which would have rendered a
literal %1$d%% wherever the English string was in effect. So the parameterised
wording gets its own name, min_playback_duration_summary, used by the summary
line; the dialog and every existing translation keep the string they had.
