From adc19d14959f24929fbbad52332af0a3d662618f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:39:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 038/547] Restore the artist queries the stats fix deleted

:app:compileCoreReleaseKotlin failed with a page of unresolved references -
artistByName, searchArtistSongs, artist - across DatabaseDao, AlbumsDao,
MediaLibrarySessionCallback, ArtistMenu and LocalSearchViewModel, plus a long
cascade of "cannot infer type" errors downstream of them.

"Fix the stats charts" meant to replace one query, mostPlayedArtists, with a
version that reads the event table. It replaced the whole Gets region of
ArtistsDao instead, taking ten unrelated queries with it: artist, artistById,
artistByName, localArtistsByNameFuzzy, searchArtists, searchLocalArtists,
searchArtistSongs, artistsByNameFuzzy, allRemoteArtists and allLocalArtists.
Nothing about the stats charts needed any of them.

They are restored exactly as the base declares them; the new mostPlayedArtists
is untouched. Checked the rest of the patch the same way - every function the
DAO layer declared at 03099c6 is still declared, so this file was the only
casualty.

Worth noting why it took three builds to find: the earlier failures in
:shazamkit and in resource merging both happen before the app module's Kotlin
is compiled, so this had been broken since the stats commit and could not
surface until those were out of the way.
