From 7e7c02744b09806f6ec93595a0080bbe69f4b7a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:17:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 052/547] Fix the top bar landing under the status bar, and the
 tablet rail covering the search bar

Two separate inset bugs in SearchBarContainer, both stemming from the
one TopAppBarScrollBehavior it shares with every screen's own
TopAppBar (e.g. ArtistItemsScreen's Playlists tab):

- Navigating Artist -> Playlists -> back to a tab route left the icon
  row rendering for a frame with the heightOffset that scrolling the
  Playlists list left on the shared scrollBehavior, appearing stuck up
  under the status bar. The correction lived in a LaunchedEffect,
  whose coroutine dispatch isn't guaranteed to land before that
  frame's layout - moved it into a remember(key) block so it runs
  synchronously in the same composition pass.

- searchBarInset/iconRowInset branched only on tabMode(), dropping the
  Start inset whenever tabMode() was true - but the nav rail is also
  shown on a tablet in landscape (useNavRail = !tabMode || isLandscape
  in MainActivity), so the rail drew over the search bar there. Thread
  useNavRail through and check it alongside tabMode().
