From 5fbeffca2f023b83af7a95adee9f871c58b8d1af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:56:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 054/547] Fix the black-screen player backgrounds, and give
 FOLLOW_THEME a renderer

Two bugs behind "the screens are all black":

- The colour-extraction LaunchedEffect skipped entirely under power
  saver, which left gradientColors permanently empty for as long as
  power saver stayed on - not just a slower animation but nothing
  drawn at all for GRADIENT and LIQUID. The extraction itself is one
  cheap Palette pass over a 100x100 bitmap; it's the ongoing Liquid
  animation that's actually expensive, and that already gates itself
  through `isActive`. Stop skipping extraction; keep gating the
  animation.

- FOLLOW_THEME had no rendering branch at all, so it always fell
  through to the plain elevated-surface Box background, solid
  near-black in dark theme. Give it one: two soft, offset blotches of
  the cover's two dominant colours (FollowThemeBackground.kt) rather
  than a flat blend, since blending two very different dominant
  colours is what looked wrong on some covers.

Also extend rememberPlayerOnBackgroundColor's cover-luminance check to
every style instead of just FROSTED/BLUR, since all five are now
artwork-derived - text/queue-handle colour was still following the
theme's guess for FOLLOW_THEME/GRADIENT/LIQUID instead of the actual
background it sits on.
