From 0e7f72bfe3795078c27cace7a1cf64c7d6a6b1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:20:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 063/547] Rework the equalizer panel: contrast color
 everywhere, rotary dials, compressor UI, matching transport

- Add a rotary dial control and use it for per-band frequency/gain in the band editor, plus quick bass/treble dials and an optional balance dial with a left/right readout.
- Add a settings toggle to color all of the panel's own text/icons/dials/sliders from the cover art's contrast color (on by default), applied consistently to the pull-down handle, band strip, editor, balance, compressor and transport - not just the handle.
- Give the panel a compressor section (enable switch plus threshold/ratio/attack/release/makeup sliders).
- Replace the mini transport with the exact same five controls the queue uses (shuffle, previous, play/pause, next, repeat), including the previously-missing repeat button.
- Add equalizer profile export/import to a JSON file.
