From 2793e592ec3b4673452c452c0475bcfb96784fa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:25:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 072/547] Fix EQ crackle on boosted presets: automatic headroom
 pre-gain plus soft clipping

Several adjacent bands boosted at once (Bass Boost, Loudness, Small Speakers) overlap enough that the summed signal clears 0dBFS well before any single band's own gain would suggest, and the previous hard coerceIn(-1f, 1f) turned that into audible crackle on transients.

Two changes: setSettings() now computes an automatic pre-gain (weighted mostly by the single worst boosted band, plus a smaller term for how much else is also boosted) and backs the signal off by that amount before the band cascade even runs - the same headroom a hardware/Winamp-style EQ needs whenever any band goes above zero. And the final output stage now runs through tanh instead of a hard clip, so anything that still peaks over full scale saturates smoothly instead of flat-topping.
