From f63f416be751120896d32d4e0a371213aafa2208 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:03:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 082/547] Layout editor schema v4: render individual
 transport/action buttons

- PlayerLayout.kt: bumped to SCHEMA_VERSION 4, fixed two bugs in the
  half-finished schema-4 groundwork from earlier - DEFAULT_BLOCKS was
  including all 17 BlockIds (including the 11 granular ones), which
  would have made hasGranularControls/hasGranularActions permanently
  true from app launch with no file imported at all; parse()'s backfill
  had the same problem for any imported file, since it filled in every
  missing BlockId unconditionally. Both now only backfill a group's
  members once the file already asked for at least one of them.
  parse() also now reads the "group" field.
- Player.kt: split controlsBlock's five transport buttons and the four
  action buttons into individually addressable composables
  (shuffleButtonBlock, playPauseButtonBlock, likeButtonBlock, etc.),
  wired into contentFor() for the eleven new BlockIds. controlsBlock()
  and actionsBlock() themselves are unchanged in what they render - they
  just call the same underlying pieces now, so a v3 file (or the
  built-in default) still renders identically.
  Free placement: the monolithic CONTROLS/ACTIONS entries are skipped
  once granular members exist for them, since a granular file still
  carries a backfilled-default entry for round-trip compatibility that
  would otherwise draw a second copy on screen.
  Stacked mode: blocks sharing a group id now render together as one
  row wherever the first member sits (matching the layout editor's own
  preview), instead of a general grouping mechanism not existing at
  all. PLAY_PAUSE keeps its fixed pill size within that row rather than
  being squeezed by Row weighting like the icon buttons around it.
  shows() now also force-includes PLAY_PAUSE, extending the existing
  "the play button can't be hidden" rule to its granular form.
- PlayerLayoutBlock.kt: blockTransform made internal so the new grouped-
  row rendering in Player.kt can apply a member's own scale/rotation
  without going through StackBlock's forced fillMaxWidth, which would
  have broken Row sizing for anything sharing a row with others.
