From 468599ce694f328d6e737bec45a4cad0d4b6b60b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:59:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 091/547] Make Liquid's text contrast follow the backdrop, not
 the cover art

rememberPlayerOnBackgroundColor measured the raw album cover's
brightness for every style including Liquid, but Liquid's actual
backdrop is a flat, known colour - LiquidColorScheme's surface/black/
white choice - which the cover's brightness has no particular relation
to. Choosing "black background -> dark text" this way was possible
whenever the cover happened to be light, even with the backdrop set to
black. Liquid now decides contrast directly from LiquidColorScheme
(black -> light text, white -> dark text, surface -> the same
theme-based fallback every other style already uses when it has
nothing better to measure), skipping the cover-luminance pass
entirely - there's nothing to measure when the answer is already known.
---
 .../outertune/ui/player/FrostedBackground.kt  | 39 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/ui/player/FrostedBackground.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/ui/player/FrostedBackground.kt
index 91703cd9f..8847cc884 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/ui/player/FrostedBackground.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/ui/player/FrostedBackground.kt
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ import coil3.request.allowHardware
 import coil3.toBitmap
 import com.dd3boh.outertune.constants.DarkMode
 import com.dd3boh.outertune.constants.DarkModeKey
+import com.dd3boh.outertune.constants.LiquidColorScheme
+import com.dd3boh.outertune.constants.LiquidColorSchemeKey
