From 264bea8a150563be2e9fc7f11352fd67864021cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:59:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 092/547] Fix two crashes that could abort playback/downloads
 mid-stream

format.contentLength!! in both MusicService's playback data source and
DownloadUtil's download data source crashed outright whenever YouTube
returned a format without a Content-Length - which happens for some
formats/streams, not all, so this reads as "sometimes, on some songs"
rather than a steady failure. Both sites already sit next to code that
treats the same field as nullable (DownloadUtil's own range-request
line two below uses `?: 10000000`); the FormatEntity inserts just
hadn't been updated to match. Applied the same fallback in both places
- it's stored metadata only, not depended on for the actual fetch
range, so a placeholder value costs nothing downstream.

Also bounded EqualizerAudioProcessor's per-band loop by the smaller of
the coefficients/states array sizes: bands and coefficients are two
separate @Volatile fields written one after the other by setSettings()
on the UI thread, so a profile switch that changes the band count
(e.g. importing a custom profile saved with a different band count)
could be read mid-write on the audio thread and index past whichever
array is still the old size - crashing ExoPlayer's playback thread
directly. Lower-probability trigger than the contentLength crashes,
but a real one worth closing defensively.
