thumbnail once and samples inward from each edge for solid near-black
bars (not just a dark scene - nearly every sampled pixel across a row/
column has to clear the threshold), capped at 40% trim per edge so a
photo that's simply dark near a border isn't mistaken for one that's
mostly letterboxing. When it finds real bars, the artist header now
crops to that content region and sizes itself to the cropped image's
