Subject: [PATCH 100/547] Give Liquid's Theme-surface backdrop and blobs
 distinct colour roles

Theme surface's backdrop was a tinted elevated surface, which read as
flat black regardless of elevation because Material3's dark-theme
surface tone is already close to black on its own - no amount of
primary tint blended into it looked clearly "themed". Switched the
backdrop itself to colorScheme.primary: a colour guaranteed not to
have that problem, and the large-area role by design here.

The petal's own fill would otherwise repeat that same primary over
its whole visible area, so it now uses colorScheme.secondary instead
for Theme surface specifically (LiquidBackground's new accentColor
parameter) - backdrop and shape read as two different weights of the
theme rather than the same colour twice. Black/White keep the petal
on primary, unchanged - a vivid colour against a neutral backdrop
that was never competing with itself. Spheres' own multi-colour
palette is untouched.

Contrast text for Theme surface now measures colorScheme.primary
directly (what's actually painted) instead of a since-removed tinted-
surface constant.
