A third LiquidShapeStyle alongside Petal and Spheres, styled after
real ferrofluid audio visualisers (the FAV-LE22 and similar) rather
than the theme-coloured flower/circles the other two are: a pool with
sharp spikes standing around its rim, snapping taller on bass rather
than breathing organically, plus a soft specular highlight (clipped to
the crown's own silhouette) that orbits slowly to suggest a wet,
reflective surface. Deliberately not theme-coloured - genuine
ferrofluid is black regardless of what's lighting it, and tinting it
with the accent colour would stop it looking like the reference at
all; this is the one shape/style in LiquidBackground that breaks from
"always real Material/album colour" on purpose.

Straight lineTo segments between peak/valley vertices rather than
Petal's smoothed quadratic contour - actual ferrofluid comes to sharp
points at the spikes and sharp cusps in the pool between them, so a
faceted polygon (softened only by a light blur, much less than
Petal's) is closer to the real geometry. Per-spike height variance is
a stable function of index and the composition's own seed, not of
time, so spikes read as naturally uneven rather than flickering.
