 existing source-error retry

The retry in onPlayerError (from the earlier 'Two more defenses against
error 2004' commit) re-resolves the stream URL and matches the User-Agent
to whichever client answers - which fixes a rejected/expired URL or a UA
mismatch, but does nothing if the real problem is YouTube's bot-detection
having flagged this client's identity: a differently-resolved URL under
the *same* identity gets the same treatment. rotateSessionIdentity() mints
a fresh visitorData (mirroring Settings > Experimental > "Delete
VisitorData") and invalidates the cached WebView PoToken session, and now
runs alongside the existing retry rather than instead of it.

Also adds resetYouTubeSessionAndRetry() as a manual escape hatch, wired to
a renamed "Reset YouTube session" entry in Experimental Settings (previously
just deleted the VisitorData preference key and relied on App's reactive
collector to notice - which left songUrlCache/retriedAfterSourceError
completely untouched, so a retry could still resolve straight back to a
cached, already-rejected URL). This clears both, rotates identity, and
retries whatever is currently loaded immediately.

