From d8adc64bf15a31112b8edd7045c9bf0f32dd2b0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 118/547] Validate streams with a ranged GET past the first
 chunk

validateStatus() issued a HEAD. googlevideo answers HEAD with 200 on
URLs whose ranged GET continuations return 403, so the check was a false
positive: whichever client was tried first always "passed" and broke out
of the fallback loop, leaving the remaining clients unreachable no
matter how broken the winning stream was. Matching the User-Agent (added
earlier in this series) narrowed that, but did not fix it - a HEAD with
the right UA still doesn't exercise a continuation request.

Probes at PROBE_OFFSET instead, which is the request that actually
fails during playback.

Also drops the unconditional break for the last fallback client. With a
probe that reflects reality there is no reason to accept an unvalidated
stream, and doing so reintroduces exactly the false pass this removes.
