From 03e25f0abb1b44cf0bbf0a06e3669a2154f94530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:35:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 126/547] Exclude the top system bar from the free-placement
 player area

Free-placement blocks (PlayerLayoutBlock's FreeBlock) measure
xPercent/yPercent against whatever size the player's content Column
reports. That Column excluded the horizontal system bar insets but not
the top one, so yPercent=0 landed under the status bar/notch instead of
at the actual top of the visible player area - a layout produced by the
standalone editor (which has no way to know this app-specific offset)
would then render everything shifted down from where it was placed.

Documented the full "player area" convention (system bars on every side,
further trimmed at the bottom by the queue peek) on PlayerLayout.Block's
xPercent/yPercent so the editor can match it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
