From 82629577abc5af685e4e5bb067edcde8eb46c2a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:57:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 129/547] Add an Equalizer settings sub-page

The dials-vs-sliders, contrast-color, and color-by-value toggles - and
profile save/load/delete - previously only existed inside the in-player
EQ panel, with no persistent Settings home. New settings/player/equalizer
screen (linked from Player settings) reads/writes the exact same
preference keys the panel does, so a change from either place stays in
sync; profile management is a separate implementation from the panel's
because the panel pushes changes live to a bound player service, which
this screen may be opened without.

Also adds an AutoEQ entry point (search field + a real dialog) as a
framework for later - actually fetching AutoEq's results database and
mapping its curve format onto this app's bands is left as a TODO, noted
in the dialog's own doc comment.

