From 9432413a08abda047ed9b4197e94fb76e6b592ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:09:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 130/547] Split combined "X & Y" credits and add featured
 artists, once verified

Two cases where a song's credited artists were less complete than YTM
actually knows: a single combined credit like "X & Y" that isn't a real
channel (no navigationEndpoint - stored with a generated local id, see
ArtistEntity.isYouTubeArtist), and an artist named in the title's
"(feat. X, Y)"/"(ft. X)" text but missing from the credited list.

New ArtistCreditEnricher.enrich(): splits a combined credit on "&" and
searches each half; only rewrites the credit into separate artists if
every half resolves to a real channel, so a genuine single-name act
whose real channel name happens to contain "&" is never incorrectly
split. Separately parses feat./ft. text out of the title and adds any
named artist not already credited, again only once a search confirms
it's real. Both checks are cheap no-ops for a song with neither pattern
- no network calls happen unless there's actually something to check.

Wired into MusicService.recoverSong() (runs once per playback, alongside
the existing related-songs/duration enrichment already there) and
DownloadUtil.scanDownloads() (a fire-and-forget batch pass over every
downloaded song, so re-running "refresh downloads" also re-checks these).

