Two related fixes for the same underlying failure mode (a resolved
stream URL going bad - "Could not find deobfuscation function" during
playback, or a silent permanent failure during downloads, both via the
same YTPlayerUtils/SignatureCipherManager pipeline):

- The bundled player_configs.json (from ZemerTeam/zemer-cipher) is a
  build-time snapshot; YouTube rotates its player far more often than
  this app ships releases, so once the current player's hash falls out
  of that snapshot, CipherWebView has no config to run and WEB
  deobfuscation fails outright until the next update. PlayerCipherConfigStore
  now layers a runtime-fetched, disk-cached copy of the same upstream file
  over the bundled one: refreshed once per cold start, and on-demand
  (rate limited) whenever a hash comes back unknown.

- Downloads resolve their stream URL through the identical pipeline and
  cache it (songUrlCache) for reuse across the file's chunks. A 403/410
  from googlevideo.com meant that cached URL was now dead, but nothing
  ever invalidated it, so every retry (Media3's own included) kept
  reusing the same known-bad URL forever. DownloadUtil now detects that
  response-code pair anywhere in the failure's cause chain and drops the
  cache entry so the next attempt re-resolves fresh.

Also adds a .gitattributes normalization rule (some edits earlier this
session picked up CRLF from a Windows/core.autocrlf interaction) so this
class of corruption can't recur silently on future edits.
