From b7edc3c361b2d91330e58db4077d7e5b7099b49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:03:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 145/547] Add crossfade with a configurable fade-out duration

There's one ExoPlayer, not two, so this isn't a true overlapping crossfade -
Crossfader instead fades the current track's volume out over the last
[setting] seconds before it ends and fades the next one back in over its own
first [setting] seconds, mirroring how SleepTimer's own fade-out already
combines into the player's volume. A track shorter than twice the configured
duration never reaches full volume, same as every other player's version of
this same shortcut.

New "Crossfade"/"Crossfade duration" entries sit in Player & audio > Playback
behaviour, next to minimum playback duration.
