 doesn't exist, not just add around it

The previous version never touched a song's own "X & Y" combined credit,
only ever adding the split-out real artists behind it - meant to avoid
losing a credit to a wrong search match, but it left the fake placeholder
sitting there permanently even once X and Y were both confirmed real, and
never linked "X & Y" itself in the (rarer) case where that's an act's actual
name.

Now: resolve "X & Y" itself first - if it's a real, populated channel, link
to that instead of the local placeholder. Only once confirmed it ISN'T a
real artist on its own does it get removed and replaced with whichever of
X/Y individually resolve to a real, populated channel (an unresolved half is
dropped too, never kept as an unconfirmed guess). Rewrites the full credit
list from scratch when anything changes rather than patching positions in
place, since the count of replacement artists can differ from one.
---
