Subject: [PATCH 151/547] Add automatic backup, so song stats survive an
 uninstall without a manual step

Backup and Restore already covers every setting and the whole database
(including play counts/listen history) - it copies the settings DataStore
file and the whole song.db wholesale, not an enumerated list of keys, so
nothing new ever needed adding there. What it didn't have was a way to run
without the user manually tapping Backup and picking a destination each
time - SAF's file-picker launchers can't run unattended, so stats (and
everything else) only ever left app-private storage - wiped on uninstall -
when someone remembered to do it themselves.

Automatic backup reuses the exact same backup format (extracted the manual
Backup action's zip-writing into writeBackup(), shared by both), written on
its own into a folder the user grants persistent SAF access to once, on a
configurable interval (default daily). Checked once whenever MusicService
starts rather than on a perpetual timer - plenty for something measured in
days - and keeps only the 5 newest automatic backups so it doesn't grow
unbounded. New "Automatic backup" section in Settings > Backup and restore:
folder picker, on/off switch, frequency, and a last-run timestamp.
