From beb60ad104f181e9bb32fd188f497b37625b05a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:55:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 152/547] Auto-create the automatic backup folder, add interval
 units, and selective categories

Replaces the SAF folder picker with Downloads/OuterTune Backup, created on
its own via MediaStore the first time an automatic backup runs - no dialog
for something that's supposed to run unattended, and no new permission
either (this app otherwise avoids broad storage access entirely; MediaStore
can create/reuse a subfolder under Downloads without it). Unavailable below
Android 10, where that API doesn't exist - the switch stays disabled there
rather than promising something that silently won't run.

Interval is now a count of days/weeks/months instead of a fixed unit, and
retention is a configurable "keep the newest N" (was hardcoded to 5).

Automatic backups can now selectively drop optional data before writing:
listen/search history, local-only playlists, synced playlists, and play
stats each have their own toggle, applied by opening the checkpointed
database copy directly and deleting the corresponding tables/rows before
zipping - the manual Backup action is untouched and always writes
everything, since that's specifically what someone reaches for to be sure
they have a complete copy.
