From c0a3db336bb57af5408dc3e528903d64ba47e04b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:32:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 159/547] Move automatic backup off the playback path onto
 WorkManager

writeAutoBackup (a WAL checkpoint plus a full copy of the live database)
used to run from a coroutine MusicService launched every time it started,
whenever the configured auto-backup interval had elapsed. That meant the
one moment this could stall - contending with the database for the
checkpoint, then copying the whole file over storage I/O - was exactly the
moment someone had just pressed play.

Replaces that trigger with a WorkManager PeriodicWorkRequest
(AutoBackupWorker), scheduled from App.kt whenever the auto-backup setting
changes (and reconciled once at cold start too, since the collector fires
immediately with whatever is currently stored). This runs on the system's
own background job scheduler - never while the app is the thing the user
is actively waiting on - and survives process death and reboots on its
own, which the old "check once when the service happens to start" approach
never did either.

AutoBackupWorker opens its own short-lived MusicDatabase instance (same
song.db file, same migration chain) rather than trying to share the live
singleton, since a background worker has no reason to hold a database
connection open past this one run.
