From 9e5c06ab287824c8c22e1428da591d4a1f803b68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:33:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 160/547] Fix a torn-snapshot race in writeBackup, and merge
 duplicate artists more completely

writeBackup ran PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(FULL) and then copied song.db as a
raw file, with nothing holding a lock across the gap between the two.
Checkpointing only guarantees the WAL is flushed into the main file at the
moment it runs - WAL mode exists specifically so writers don't have to
wait on that, so another write (a play count, a download's state) could
land in the file while the copy was still streaming it. A copy caught
mid-write isn't a smaller backup, it's a torn one: it can fail the restore
path's integrity check, or worse, silently load a partially-written
database. This affected the original manual backup feature too, not just
the automatic-backup addition.

Fixed by adding MusicDatabase.runInTransaction, a synchronous wrapper
around Room's own RoomDatabase.runInTransaction (unlike the existing
`transaction` helper, which fires asynchronously on Room's own executor
and can't be awaited). writeBackup now runs the checkpoint and the file
copy inside it, holding the database's single writer connection for the
whole copy - typically well under a second - so the bytes on disk can't
move while they're being read. Readers elsewhere are unaffected, since WAL
mode never blocks those on a writer.

Separately: MIGRATION_23_24 only ever merges a "- Topic" row into an
already clean-named row. Real libraries end up with duplicate artist rows
for reasons that have nothing to do with the Topic suffix at all - the
same artist getting a different generated id from two different sync
paths - and even within the Topic-suffix case specifically, two "- Topic"
rows with no clean row to merge into each just got renamed in place
independently, leaving two identical-looking duplicates behind. Adds
MIGRATION_24_25 (mergeDuplicateArtists), which groups every artist row by
its Topic-stripped, lowercased name and merges each group of 2+ down to
one, regardless of which rows happen to carry the suffix.

Also fixes two smaller spots that never went through the shared
stripTopicSuffix() dedup: ArtistsDao.update(artist, artistPage) was
writing an artist-page title verbatim, and LyricsHelper had its own
separate, weaker ad hoc strip (case-sensitive removeSuffix(" - Topic"),
no regex) for building lyrics search queries.
