From 4f6d1f54b689e08bc707f28a16610ac336bc29e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:33:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 161/547] Add a way to move already-downloaded songs to a new
 folder

Changing the external download folder in Settings has never actually
moved anything: swapping DownloadPathKey only changes where new downloads
and rescans look, and leaves every file already in the old folder orphaned
there. migrateDownloads() doesn't cover this either - it's a one-time
convert from the old internal ExoPlayer cache format to external files,
not a general folder-to-folder move.

Adds DownloadUtil.moveDownloads(oldDirUri, newDirUri), which copies every
file (songs and, if enabled, thumbnails) out of the old folder into the
new one via SAF, deleting each source file only after its own copy has
landed - so a picker choice that turns out read-only, or a copy that fails
partway, leaves files in their original folder rather than losing them.

Wired into Storage settings as a new "Move downloads to a new folder..."
entry: picks the destination, confirms with both paths shown, shows
live copy progress, then updates DownloadPathKey and rescans once the
move finishes.
