From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:44:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 163/547] Tighten the proactive stream-URL refresh window to
 20s

Field reports of playback dying with a source error around ~30s in,
audibly self-healing via the existing onPlayerError retry rather than
being silently avoided by the proactive refresh. The 40s trust window
was sized against a cutoff earlier testing placed at roughly a minute;
if that cutoff has since tightened toward ~30s, the old window loses the
race more often than not. Keeps roughly the same proportional safety
margin against the new, lower estimate instead of the original one.
Not a confirmed root cause - a conservative tightening pending logs from
an actual SERVICE_DEBUG-enabled repro if it keeps happening.

