From 0d85cb14ed7e6aaaf3e1e2c803ffb0d3e998f4e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:43:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 166/547] Fix a race in move-downloads that could re-point
 localMgr at the old folder

The move handler called onDownloadPathChange(newUri) - rememberPreference's
MutableState setter, which fires the DataStore write on its own
composition-scoped coroutine and returns immediately - then called
downloadUtil.cd() right after in a different coroutine, with nothing
guaranteeing the write had landed first. If cd() won that race, it would
re-init localMgr from the still-stale DownloadPathKey, pointing it at the
old folder - now emptied by the move that just finished - making every
downloaded song look missing until something else happened to re-run cd().

Writes directly to the DataStore and suspends on it in the same coroutine
instead, so cd() is guaranteed to see the new path. The Compose-displayed
downloadPath still updates correctly either way, since it's collecting the
same underlying DataStore flow regardless of which code wrote to it.

