From 9ea6b990df42256a0a7114b96124bd1fcb02a0b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:23:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 179/547] Write the artist's current name back to the library
 when its page is opened

Tapping an artist credited as "X" on a song could land on a page headed "Y".
ArtistScreen shows artistPage.artist.title - the authoritative name straight
from YouTube - in preference to the stored one, but nothing ever wrote that
name back, so the library row kept whatever it was first created with and
every song credit went on showing the old name indefinitely.

The only refresh that existed ran from the Library and Stats screens, and
only for artists with no thumbnail or not touched in 10 days, so opening the
artist page - the one place the fresh name is already in hand - never fixed
it.

ArtistViewModel now updates the stored artist after a successful fetch, via
the existing ArtistsDao.update(artist, artistPage) (which already strips the
"- Topic" suffix, so this doesn't reintroduce those). Because the song credit
renders from ArtistEntity.name through SongArtistMap, correcting the one row
fixes every credit for that artist at once.

Only writes when the name or picture actually differs, so lastUpdateTime
isn't churned on every visit, and reads the current row straight from the
database rather than from libraryArtist.value - that flow is
SharingStarted.Lazily and this runs right after init's fetch, so its cached
value can still be null for an artist that is in fact in the library, which
would have made the whole thing silently do nothing.
