From ef33ea626d414f4ef848d0c74b0bd60844a17ace Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:16:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 181/547] Send a PoToken with VISIONOS's player request, so it
 stops being bot-blocked

Captured over adb, on every track without exception:

  [VISIONOS] rejected: playabilityStatus=LOGIN_REQUIRED
             - Sign in to confirm you're not a bot
  [VISIONOS] trying stream client: WEB_REMIX
  RESOLVED via WEB_REMIX, expires in 21540s

So VISIONOS was reached, its response parsed, and the host routing was fine -
YouTube simply refused it, and playback fell to WEB_REMIX and its ~60s URLs
exactly as before. Every earlier fix this session was aimed at the wrong
thing because none of them had this line to go on.

VISIONOS has loginSupported = false, so its player request carried no cookie
and no PoToken - a fully anonymous request, which is what draws that
challenge once a session or address has been flagged. Authenticated
WEB_REMIX passing while every anonymous client is challenged is the
signature of that. A PoToken is the mechanism the challenge exists to be
