A WEB_REMIX stream this video just had rejected was being skipped
entirely on the retry, on the theory that the retry should reach a
fallback client instead of repeating the same failure. That reasoning
only holds if a fallback can actually serve the track, and here none
can: every anonymous client in the chain is refused with a bot
challenge, because the PoToken this app can mint is a web token from
the WebView's BotGuard and is not valid for VISIONOS, ANDROID_VR or
IOS. Removing the one client YouTube will serve therefore guaranteed
the retry failed - the log shows it burning through five dead clients
and then stopping playback outright.

Last place in the order keeps the "prefer a fallback" intent without
betting the whole retry on a fallback existing. Re-requests the player
response in that case rather than reusing the one fetched for metadata,
since reusing it would hand back the very url that was just rejected -
a fresh url is the entire point of retrying when the cause was a stale
or wrongly-bound one.
