split returns a one-element list and the index throws. innertubex does
report the codecs, just as a separate field, so the adapter now composes
the two into the shape the rest of the app already expects.

The crash landed inside database.query { upsert(FormatEntity(...)) },
which is what made it look unrelated to downloading: the audio file
finished and was cached, then the process died before the download status
was written. Media3's index said COMPLETED while the database said
nothing had been downloaded - songs listed under Downloaded with no
downloaded icon, and re-requesting did nothing because the download
already existed. scanDownloads() on next launch rebuilds status from that
index, so the state repairs itself once the crash stops.

All three call sites now use getOrNull(1) as well. Any format lacking a
codecs parameter crashed them regardless of what produced it, so the
adapter fix removes this instance and this removes the class of it.

