The blobs were rendering as flat black. baseColor was passed the surface
role straight through, and in a dark scheme that role is already
near-black, so the lit term had nothing of the theme left in it to carry -
the body read as a hole in the background rather than an object in it.

Blends black with the accent instead, black-dominant so the material
still reads as ink: the unlit faces stay black and the lit ones pick up
enough of the current theme to belong to it. Kept well down at 0.18;
past roughly a fifth it stops looking like ferrofluid and starts looking
like coloured plastic.

The specular and Fresnel terms are untouched - those were already themed
and were the only colour in there before.
