From 7196c1003865f631376a5d094138d227afcca926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 09:42:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 197/547] Group the appearance settings by subject instead of
 by leftovers

The screen already drew its groups as cards, so the problem was not the
boxes but what was in them: "Display" had become the place things went
when they did not obviously belong anywhere else. It held tab extras, the
slim navbar, two artwork switches, the top bar logo, the player
background, the player layout link and the app icon - eight controls
across five unrelated subjects, under a heading that predicted none of
them.

Six groups now, each named for what is actually inside it:

  Theme        theme and accent
  Layout       tab arrangement, tab extras, slim navbar - all "where the
               app puts you and how you move around it"
  Now playing  player background and player layout
  Thumbnails   high-res artwork and its low-res fallback, kept adjacent
               so the dependency between them is visible rather than
               inferred
  General      top bar logo, app icon
  Behavior     gestures

All six titles are existing strings, so nothing here needs retranslating.

Adds SettingsGroup for the title/card/spacer trio every settings screen
was spelling out by hand, which is why grouping was a matter of
remembering to repeat three things in the right order and why the
trailing spacer was easy to omit. Only this screen is converted - the
other eleven can adopt it as they are touched, rather than churning them
all while a release is being tested.
