From 9af725a4b78097ddeb316a258a13a9f4b18f0233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:37:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 199/547] Bind the stream url's PoToken to the video id, as
 innertubex requires

Playback died with a 403 on a media request - about a minute in on most
tracks, immediately on some - and every download failed the same way.
Metrolist, on the same account and device, was fine.

Logcat showed every single resolve coming back as WEB_REMIX (WEB_REMIX__po)
from MetrolistStreamResolver, and the range shape was not the cause:
innertubex's own requiresBoundedMediaRange/usesChunkedMediaRanges agree
with StreamRangePolicy that a web client is read straight through, so
withResolvedStream applies no bound to it at all.

The tokens were crossed. PoTokenResult's fields are named for the roles
the native client loop gives them - playerRequestPoToken holds the
video-id-bound token, streamingDataPoToken the visitorData-bound one -
and the innertubex bridge passed them through by name. But innertubex
names its two by the request they ride on and decides the binding itself:
PlaybackClientCatalog gives WEB_REMIX webGvsRequired, which is
PoTokenRule(REQUIRED, VIDEO_ID), so the token on the stream url has to be
bound to the video id, not to visitorData. So the url was signed with the
wrong one. That is not refused at resolve time - the url looks fine coming
back - which is why it surfaced as a 403 partway into playback, and on
every download, since a download reads the whole file.

Mapping them by binding rather than by field name leaves the native
path's own orientation untouched.

Also stop accepting a WEB_REMIX stream from the resolver when this video
just had one rejected. innertubex answers WEB_REMIX for essentially every
track, so it ran ahead of the client loop and handed the same url back:
MusicService's retry dropped the cached url, called
markWebRemixStreamFailed, re-resolved, and got the identical rejection,
never reaching the loop that would have tried VISIONOS and validated the
result. The deprioritisation that was already written could not take
effect. Anything else innertubex resolves is still taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
