From 4b7b77873f8cbdf39fb39ee92f3221df6c637a36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:30:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 204/547] Point the cipher config table at a url that exists

The configured source was

  cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/MetrolistGroup/faraday@main/registry/player_configs.json

and it has answered 404 to every request this app has ever made, because
faraday's default branch is master and there is no main ref to resolve.
The file itself is real - the same path on master returns 47KB - so this
was one wrong word in a url, not a missing registry.

Nothing surfaced it. A config table that fails to load does not stop
playback; it leaves signature and n-parameter handling on whatever can be
managed locally, and the result reads as an ordinary rejected stream. So
the app has been resolving every stream without the table whose entire
purpose is to keep deobfuscation working across a player rotation.

Switched to the table Metrolist consumes rather than fixing the branch.
Both registries were fetched and compared: faraday carries 322 players,
zemer 326, each holds a handful the other does not, and both currently
describe the player YouTube is serving (e937390a) with identical sig,
nClass, sts and aliases fields. So this is not a coverage decision. It is
worth more to be reading the same source as an app that demonstrably
works on this account, so that a future failure can be compared like for
like instead of confounded by two different tables.

Fetched from raw.githubusercontent rather than a CDN deliberately.
jsDelivr caches a branch ref for hours, and the whole value of this table
is being republished promptly when YouTube rotates its player - serving a
stale copy across a rotation reintroduces exactly what it exists to
prevent.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
