From c04f5f4191f20786cd318bf1207884a470e3f108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:54:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 207/547] Plant a Timber tree, and merge download headers
 instead of replacing them

Two follow-ups from the first logcat of the ported engine.

Timber had no tree planted, so every one of the ~300 log calls in the
imported cipher and PoToken stack was discarded. The engine worked and
said nothing: no CipherDeobfuscator init, no config table sizes, no
PoToken output. Reading exactly those lines out of Metrolist's release
build is what made this diagnosable in the first place, so the tree is
planted unconditionally rather than only in debug builds, which is what
Metrolist does too.

DownloadUtil replaced the DataSpec's request headers with the stream's
instead of merging them, in both the cached and freshly-resolved
branches. Metrolist v13.6.3 merges in both - dataSpec.httpRequestHeaders
+ streamHeaders - and replacing discards whatever the caller had already
put on the spec. That is a plausible reason a download 403s on a url the
player is streaming happily at the same moment, which is the remaining
symptom: playback is fine and most downloads now succeed, but a few come
back 403 and are then dropped by the invalid-state handler rather than
retried.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
