From 039434c42d58b77c2c05a7c70a8d0a9892fa183e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:35:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 212/547] Give an album its artists back from its own tracks

The mirror of the song-takes-from-album fallback, for the case where the
album is the side missing the data. YTM returns some albums with no
artist at all, which leaves them uncredited everywhere they are listed
even though every track on them names the same artist.

Only artists credited on every track are used. Taking one track's credits
would be wrong on anything that is not a single-artist record: on a
compilation, or on an album carrying one guest feature, whichever track
happened to be looked at would put its guest on the album as though they
had made all of it. An intersection can only yield artists the whole
record shares - on a normal album exactly its artist, and on a
compilation correctly nothing, which is left alone rather than guessed
at.

Runs only when the album has no artists at all, so it never argues with
data YTM did supply. It cannot recurse into the song-side fallback
either: that one returns before reaching this, and only ever runs for a
song with no artists, which contributes nothing to an intersection.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

