From 67e3d17585e0bd36313998fe2fb85a2ef3d22afd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:55:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 221/547] Treat MPLAUC and UC as the one artist they are

The enricher's own log gave this away:

  enriching "Gimme Dat Love": i-dle(MPLAUCWT2ZfW7d8YI-HinHEVhyCA), i-dle(UCWT2ZfW7d8YI-HinHEVhyCA)

Those are the same channel. YTM returns an artist under a plain channel
id in some responses and under a browse id that is that same channel id
with MPLA stuck on the front in others, and nothing here knew the two
were related.

That is both of the artist complaints at once, not two.

The duplicate credit is one artist arriving twice under two spellings.
And "is this a real channel" is decided by the id starting with UC, which
the prefixed form fails - so it was filed as a local placeholder and
rendered greyed out and untappable. A song credited only under the
prefixed form therefore had no working artist link at all, which no
amount of de-duplicating could have fixed, because there was no twin to
keep.

Normalised rather than tolerated: the enricher rewrites a prefixed credit
to the bare id, which makes it a real channel and makes it collide with
its own twin instead of showing alongside it. isYouTubeArtist and
hasArtistPage also accept the prefixed form, so a credit that has not
been through the enricher yet is at least tappable in the meantime. And
YouTube.artist strips the prefix before browsing, since only the bare
form resolves - done at the one place that fetches an artist page rather
than at every screen that navigates to one.

Also finishes the UK spelling pass. The equalizer panel's "Color by
value" was hardcoded in Kotlin rather than in strings.xml, which is why
it survived a sweep of the string resources - along with three
"Prioritize" strings and "licenses", which is a noun here.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

