From 30e1505ca0c0bed7b64234d35c2f980f48a64710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:14:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 222/547] Stop a bare "- Topic" channel overwriting the name it
 has no name for

A regression from the stripTopicSuffix fix, caught before it could bite.

That fix stopped a channel titled exactly "- Topic" reducing to an empty
string, because stripping is meant to tidy a name rather than delete one.
But two places write a name straight from the stripped page title, and
both were relying on the old empty result to protect them: ArtistViewModel
guarded on isNotBlank, and ArtistsDao.update wrote unconditionally. With
the suffix now surviving the strip, the guard passes and the write goes
through - so opening such a channel's page would have renamed a correctly
stored "Seraphine" to "- Topic".

The suffix surviving the strip is exactly the tell that there was nothing
in front of it, so both places now keep the stored name in that case. The
DAO matters as much as the caller, because it is the write: a refresh that
only intended to update the picture would otherwise have taken the name
down with it.

Also compares normalised ids when working out which artists an album's
tracks share. A record whose tracks credit the same artist under both id
spellings shares that artist on every track and, to a raw id comparison,
looked like it shared nobody - which is what "tracks share no artist" was
reporting for albums that plainly have one.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

