From e569fb9bf6d2c13b4066b3443e555e2035008deb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:40:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 229/547] Make the fluid break up and remerge, and stop linking
 to Topic channels

The ferrofluid renderer modelled the wrong phenomenon. The Rosensweig
instability - a static field throwing a flat pool into a hexagonal lattice
of spikes - is real ferrofluid behaviour, but it is not what the footage
people mean shows, which is a free-floating mass breaking into droplets and
flowing back together. So the lattice and the cone SDF are gone.

The break-up is emergent rather than animated. Every droplet shares one
slow breathing cycle that pushes it out from a central core and draws it
back, and since the smin blend radius is fixed, that single number decides
whether neighbours are within blend range: close together they fuse into
one connected mass, far apart they separate into beads with necks
stretching and snapping between them. A small per-droplet phase offset
means they do not all part company on the same frame, so the mass tears
raggedly rather than blooming open.

This is also cheaper, which the previous version needed to be. Spheres cost
less than cones, the second specular lobe is gone, the bounding sphere
shrank 1.45 -> 1.25, and the default tier drops to 6 droplets at 0.42 scale
and 24fps. Diffuse is now wrapped, which stops the far side of a droplet
going flat black.

The material is tinted considerably harder towards the theme colour. That
is deliberately against physical accuracy - ferrofluid is black - but a
black shape on a dark UI is a hole, and the highlight, Fresnel edge and
reflected gradient are what identify the material anyway.

Separately: resolveArtist took the first search result matching the name,
which was a coin flip between the artist's real channel and the
auto-generated "X - Topic" one. The Topic channel is only a bucket for
auto-uploads - no About, no meaningful subscriber count, often not even the
full discography - so linking a song to it produces a much worse artist
page for no reason. The real channel is now preferred, falling back to
Topic only when that is all that exists. Duplicate-credit resolution reads
through the same function, so it inherits this.

Verified by compiling coreRelease. The AGSL compiles on device, not at
build time; it falls back to the Canvas version on failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
