From 64accc289567f8b0a0dbf4a6d4959b19d8fbc7f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:18:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 236/547] Fix five faults found reviewing the recent work

Swipe-to-remove in the queue used the row index as a queue index. While a
queue search is active the list renders filteredSongs, so that index
belongs to the filtered list - swiping removed whichever song happened to
sit at that position in the real queue instead of the one swiped. This one
predates the undo work but the undo inherited it, and restored the wrong
song to match. It now takes the song and resolves the index by identity.

The ferrofluid frame cap reset the clock. Its start timestamp is a local of
the effect, so pausing and resuming - or changing quality, which restarts
the effect too - took the scene back to t=0 and snapped every droplet
somewhere else. The accumulating loop it replaced did not do this. The
elapsed clock is now anchored to where it already was.

Preferring a real channel over a Topic one compared a title to its own
stripped form. stripTopicSuffix deliberately returns its input unchanged
when stripping would leave nothing, so a channel titled exactly "- Topic"
compared equal and read as a real channel - the single case the preference
exists to avoid. Tested against the suffix directly now.

Cache promotion had to move enqueueing off the main thread, and it went
onto the shared download dispatcher, which runs several jobs at once. A
promotion takes as long as the song is big, so a playlist queued through it
reached Media3 in whatever order the copies finished. Enqueueing now has
one lane; these are local disk copies and do not go faster in parallel.

album_artist_map.artistId is a foreign key onto artist.id, and the album
backfill normalises the id as it inserts. A channel held only under the
MPLAUC spelling has no bare-id row until mergePrefixedArtists runs, and
enrich can reach an album before that happens - so the insert could point
at a parent that does not exist. The artist row is now inserted first, as
IGNORE, so an artist already in the library keeps the row it has. Latent
rather than observed, and older than the reconcile work built on top of it.

Also corrects a comment that claimed the word-sync sweep pauses between
words. It does not: consecutive words get touching time ranges, so a word
holds the highlight for its whole slice and the gap is crossed at the
boundary.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

