From f6a9156d565f96289bcbc6e8d2ef55d629901c36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:29:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 237/547] Keep the now-playing marker on its song while the
 queue is being reordered

Dragging reorders the on-screen list immediately but deliberately leaves
the player alone until the drop. Both the now-playing animation and the
tap-to-toggle check were matching on row position against the player's
current index, so for the whole duration of a drag that index pointed at
whichever song had been shuffled into the slot - the animation jumped to a
song that was not playing, while the one that was carried on playing
without it.

Matched on the song's uid now. It is stamped from the player's own index
when the list is built, so it still identifies the right row mid-drag, and
unlike an id comparison it tells two copies of the same song apart.

The list also scrolled to the playing song every time the queue changed at
all, which includes a change the user just made by hand: drop a song
somewhere and the list would immediately yank away to wherever the playing
song was, so the one place you were certainly looking was the one place it
would not leave you. It now scrolls only when the song being played
actually changes, which is the case that wanted it.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

