From 3dd3213b9d37302327ac778cab5710c4337883a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:59:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 240/547] Stop the queue flashing on drop, and let it fill the
 width in landscape

Two queue faults and one layout one.

Dropping a dragged song made the whole list flash. The queue rebuild clears
and refills the list from the player whenever the timeline changes, and
each entry is stamped with a uid taken from its index - which the
LazyColumn keys off. So after a reorder every row got a new key and counted
as a brand new item, even though the list on screen was already in exactly
the right order: the drag had put it there, and the player was only told
afterwards. The rebuild is now skipped when the queue's contents already
match what is shown, which is precisely the reorder case.

That means uids no longer track indices after a reorder, so the now-playing
marker cannot be found by uid any more. It is held as the list entry
itself, assigned only from the player's own state and never in response to
the list being rearranged - so the marker travels with the song as it is
dragged, which is what it always looked like it should do.

In tab mode the queue padded itself with the player-aware insets, and those
carry the navigation rail's width so ordinary screens lay out beside it.
The queue is not an ordinary screen: it is drawn over the entire window,
rail included, so that reserved room for chrome that is not there and left
the queue shifted off the left edge with dead space beside it in landscape.
It uses the plain system insets now - bars and cutout, which do still have
to be avoided - the same ones the non-tab path already used.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

