From 5760bcf5aad5993a24ed400d49b8fdd77b871a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:13:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 243/547] Stop the artist page throwing away the choice to view
 the library

Tapping "from your library" appeared to hang: the tab would sit there, the
local content never arrived, and the screen stayed on the remote view that
was still loading. The local songs and albums were ready in the database
the entire time.

showLocal was assigned inside LaunchedEffect(libraryArtist), and
libraryArtist is a database flow. It re-emits whenever the artist row is
written - which happens right after the YouTube fetch lands, in
refreshLibraryArtist, and now also when the artist repair runs on launch.
Every one of those emissions overwrote the user's choice back to false, so
the tap was undone a moment later and the remote view came back.

It now picks the starting view once, when the artist row first arrives, and
never touches it again. Local artists still start on the local page, since
they have no remote one to show.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
