From 934834337b5e1331058353cebec3fdd0d286c5a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:51:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 245/547] Prove the desktop stream by fetching audio, not just
 a URL

A URL is not a stream. googlevideo hands out URLs that then answer 403 -
that is exactly the failure this fork spent weeks on, and it is invisible
at the point the URL is produced. So the probe's "USABLE" verdict was only
a claim about the player response, and until something fetched bytes there
was nothing behind it.

It fetches them now: a ranged request against the first client that
produced a URL, carrying that client's own user agent, because googlevideo
has been observed refusing a fetch whose headers do not match the client
the URL was issued to.

Result on Windows 11, plain JVM, no browser and no PoToken: HTTP 206 and
65536 bytes of audio, via IOS. Ranged rather than whole, so it proves the
CDN serves this machine without pulling a song to find out.

That settles the stream layer for a desktop port. What is left is playback
- Media3 is Android-only - the database, and the UI, none of which are
adversarial in the way the token problem looked.

