From 3e0a99a386a44aa1fc12980df566e839ed0d6fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:07:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 252/547] Add pause, by stopping the line rather than the
 decoder

A stopped SourceDataLine keeps what it has buffered and stops draining it,
so the decode loop blocks on its next write once that buffer fills and
resumes exactly where it left off when the line starts again. Nothing has
to be tracked, counted or rewound, which is why the pause lives there
rather than in a flag the decode loop checks.

Also corrects the file's own account of what is missing. It claimed no
pause, which is no longer true, and said nothing about the one real upside
of fetching a song in full before playing it: once audio starts there is no
network left to fail, so a mid-song 403 cannot happen. That is worth
recording because streaming playback would remove the initial wait and
introduce exactly that failure - it is a trade, not an improvement.

Verified by running it on Windows 11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
