From 6faa3d087f20222ccbbcfc62db6d9d93770ce7c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:32:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 258/547] Add shuffle and repeat, and somewhere to see liked
 songs

Liking a song wrote to a file and nothing ever read it back, which is a
feature that only produces a file. The home view now shows Liked above
Recently played, and playing from either queues the whole shelf rather than
one song followed by silence.

Shuffle keeps the queue's own order and shuffles a separate play order over
it, so turning shuffle on does not rearrange the list under the user and
lose the album they queued. The currently playing track is pinned to the
front of that order: shuffling the whole thing would drop it into the
middle of its own queue, and "previous" would then go somewhere it had
never been. Toggling mid-song therefore changes what comes next rather than
jumping elsewhere immediately, which is what the control is for.

Repeat cycles off, all and one. Repeat-one restarts the same track instead
of advancing, and with repeat off the end of the queue still stops rather
than wrapping - wrapping unasked is exactly what repeat exists to turn on.

Both controls sit beside the scrubber rather than with the transport
buttons, because they change what the queue does next; they do not act on
the track that is playing.

Verified by running it on Windows 11.

