From 445f073b443216f4988d70a8ade3c5091e805d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:34:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 259/547] Add keyboard control, without breaking the search box

Space plays and pauses, the arrows seek ten seconds, and the media keys do
what they say. All of it is ignored while the search field has focus, which
is the part that needed thought rather than the shortcuts themselves: space
has to keep typing a space and the arrows have to keep moving the caret. A
shortcut that eats the text field is worse than not having the shortcut.

Handled as a preview key event on the root so it is reached before the
list, and gated on the field's own focus state rather than on guesswork
about what is focused.

Verified by running it on Windows 11.

