From 900e781ac430663abceb7cc3e5afad737ead77d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:35:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 260/547] Leave a handover for whoever picks the desktop client
 up next

Records what is built, what runs it, and the four findings that were each
established by running something rather than reasoning - two of which
overturned a conclusion stated confidently and wrongly earlier, so they are
written down with the mistake attached rather than as clean facts.

Separates deliberate trades from things not yet done, because a full fetch
before playback and a text file for a library both look like shortcuts and
are not: the first buys immunity to mid-song 403s and arithmetic seeking,
the second deliberately defers a database decision that should not be made
as a side effect of wanting a recently-played list.

Also states plainly what "port the player layout" involves - 1754 lines,
108 Android imports, and a background built on RuntimeShader, which does
not exist off Android - so the next person costs that honestly instead of
starting a copy that cannot work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
