From b1e295f42a6502cd5b258cd104a0b68eac0cd562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:53:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 261/547] Lay the player out beside its cover, and fix three
 things testing found

The full player puts the cover beside the controls rather than above them.
A desktop window is wide and short, so stacking wastes the width and
squeezes the art into whatever height is left; side by side lets the cover
be as large as the window is tall.

Three fixes, all reported rather than caught here.

Songs played from the library showed "Unknown artist" while playing. The
store keeps artists as one display string, and converting back produced an
empty artist list - lossy was the intent, wrong was the result: it had the
name and declined to use it. It comes back as a single unlinked artist now.

Covers were fetched at whatever size YouTube happened to return, which for
search results is 60-226px, so anything larger than a list row was an
upscaled postage stamp. The size is part of the URL, so the drawn size is
now requested - at 2x for high-DPI, rounded to a step so a handful of sizes
are cached rather than one per pixel dimension.

The like button changed glyph with no motion, which reads as nothing
happening - it looked broken while working. It springs and animates its
colour now, on liking only; celebrating a removal is odd.

Also caps the artwork cache at 60 rather than 300. A cover is ~1.2MB
decoded, so the old bound quietly authorised 350MB of bitmaps, which is a
large part of why the app measured heavier than it should.

