From eab2414073ac8a6956d2915edef453eb38e17254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:10:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 264/547] Add a lyrics timing offset, for lyrics that are
 consistently out of step

Plenty of lyric files are uniformly early or late against the recording the
app is playing - a different master, a different edit, or simply a badly
timed transcription. Nothing could be done about it except stop using them.

An offset in milliseconds is added to the playback position everywhere it
is compared against a lyric time: the current-line search, the karaoke
sweep's seed, its scrub path and its wall-clock estimate. All four, because
missing one would leave the highlighted line and the word sweep disagreeing
with each other, which is worse than both being wrong together.

Applied to the position rather than by rewriting the timestamps. The stored
lyrics are not wrong to keep - they are only wrong to trust at face value -
and rewriting them would bake one song's correction into a file that other
songs share.

Stored per app rather than per song: the same source tends to be off by a
similar amount across a library, and a per-song value would mean setting it
again for every track. Five seconds either way; wider than that is not a
sync correction, it is the wrong lyrics file.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

