From 8e1e16d1640e047a80681d6926cd3a1d7eadc74d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:25:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 265/547] Clean every lyrics source, not just captions - but
 only the safe part

The speaker markers and music annotations that made caption tracks read
badly are not unique to captions. Any provider can return ">>" or a line
that is nothing but [Music], and it reads exactly as badly wherever it came
from. That cleanup now runs on every provider.

Split in two rather than applied wholesale, because one part of the caption
treatment must not be general. Re-breaking lines at sentence ends is right
for captions, which are broken wherever the recogniser paused and carry no
intent at all - and wrong for a real lyrics file, which is already broken
where its author meant it to be. Applied there it would cut "Hello. Is it
me you're looking for?" in half. So cleanLyrics does markers and
annotations for everyone, and cleanCaptionLyrics adds the re-breaking for
captions alone.

Done in the aggregator rather than in six providers, so there is one path
rather than six that can drift apart. It also runs before classification
and not only before storage: an annotation-only line is not evidence of
lyrics, and judging the raw text could adopt a "lyric sheet" that is
nothing but [Music] repeated.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
