From 46a52ffde1592552a4da2b858707e4c1874364ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:40:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 267/547] Fix the layout editor's icons, spacing and grouping,
 and use the app's own artwork

The control row looked messy for a reason that no amount of adjusting the
gap could fix: four icons - seek back, seek forward, sleep timer,
equalizer - were drawn on a 24x24 grid while everything else used 960. An
icon nominally "20px" on a 24 grid is enormously heavier than one on a 960
grid, so the row had five different optical weights in it. Everything is on
one grid now, and the paths for play, pause, skip, shuffle, repeat, like
and queue are lifted verbatim from the app's own res/drawable vectors, so
the preview shows the buttons the phone actually draws rather than
Material's lookalikes.

The per-control markup was a switch with sizes that had drifted apart -
28/20, 34/20, 50/26, 28/18. It is a table of three roles now: play/pause is
the primary target, the skips are solid secondary buttons, everything else
is a plain tinted glyph, and the glyph is a fixed fraction of its box in
each. The row keeps one rhythm at any scale.

Three real bugs, found by driving the page rather than reading it.

Buttons overlapped in free placement. Every block was forced to width:w%,
but a button's icon is a fixed pixel size, so a 52px play button inside a
block the layout had decided was 40px wide spilled over its neighbours.
Buttons are content-sized now, and the width slider is no longer offered
for them - it was a control that visibly did nothing.

Seeded button rows overlapped by a few pixels because the span was divided
evenly, which assumes every button is the same size when play/pause is 52px
against 30px. They are laid out edge to edge from their real widths with a
fixed gap and centred, which cannot overlap by construction. All four
presets now seed with zero overlapping pairs, verified in the browser.

Grouping the cover with the title collapsed the cover to a fifth of the
screen. Every group was treated as a row of buttons and each member given
w/max(count,4). A group is laid out as a row only when every member is
actually a button now; anything else stacks at its natural size.

Seek back and forward default to hidden, because the app ships them off - a
preset showing them was not describing the default player.

The artwork placeholder was a saturated pink-purple gradient with "ART"
written on it, which read as the loudest thing on screen - the one thing a
stand-in should never be. It is a neutral surface tone with the app's own
music-note mark, scaled with the tile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
