+
+/*
+ * Every icon on one coordinate system, and wherever possible the app's own artwork.
+ *
+ * Two things were wrong before. The transport glyphs were Material's rather than OuterTune's, so the
+ * preview showed buttons the app does not actually draw. And four of them - seek back, seek forward,
+ * sleep timer, equalizer - were drawn on a 24x24 grid while everything else used 960, which is why
+ * the control row looked uneven: an icon nominally "20px" on a 24 grid is enormously heavier than
+ * one on a 960 grid, so the row had no consistent optical weight no matter how the gaps were set.
+ *
+ * The paths marked APP are lifted verbatim from app/src/main/res/drawable, so the preview matches
+ * what the phone renders. The rest are Material Symbols on the same 960 grid, used because the app
