From 9693e943d17c759a62c4f7d7f6db69a731fb8a1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:52:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 269/547] Draw the phone's navigation, and make the aspect
 buttons actually work

Checking a layout against another shape has never worked. ASPECTS stored
its entries as `w`/`h` while activeScreen() is read as `.width`/`.height`
everywhere, so pressing an aspect button made every dimension undefined:
the preview's own size became NaN, the phone kept whatever size it already
had, and the artwork placeholder blew up because its glyph size was NaN
too. That is the "cover art icon switches to a bigger one" - the only
visible symptom of the buttons doing nothing at all. Fixed, and the preview
now genuinely reshapes: 711px tall for 20:9 down to 427px for 4:3.

The caption was no clearer. "your design is still 1080x2400" does not say
what it is telling anyone; it now says the layout is unchanged and only the
preview has been reshaped, which is the actual point.

Navigation is drawn below the player area - three marks or a gesture pill -
so the preview reads as a device rather than a floating rectangle, and so
the queue handle has something to sit above. Deliberately the same height
either way: letting the two reserve different amounts would make a layout
depend on which navigation the designer happened to use, and the same file
would then sit differently on a button phone than a gesture one. Verified
identical - 666px of player area in both. It is recorded in the exported
file and read back on import, because it is worth knowing what a layout was
drawn against even when it does not change the geometry.

Free placement now starts from the stacked layout on screen.
seedFreePositions skips any block that already has coordinates, which is
right while editing a free layout and wrong on the way in - a preset loaded
while stacked left the previous preset's coordinates untouched, so
switching to free showed the old design. Coordinates are cleared on the
transition into free only, never while already there, so an arrangement
being worked on is not thrown away by touching the mode buttons. Loading a
preset while already in free mode seeds it too, which previously appeared
to do nothing.

Verified in a browser: every aspect reshapes the preview, the artwork glyph
stays stable, the queue handle never overlaps the navigation strip, and
loading two different presets into free mode now gives two different
arrangements.

