From 0ca97f67a812e64504c835e89cafa50119ca878a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:57:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 271/547] Keep the phone preview centred when its shape changes

Switching to a shorter ratio made the whole preview jump upward. The
preview is sized to a constant width and lets its height follow the aspect
ratio, so a 4:3 phone is nearly 300px shorter than a 20:9 one - and as a
plain flex child it shrank about its top edge, so the frame appeared to
move when only its height had changed. That reads as the page rearranging
itself rather than the phone changing shape, which is exactly the wrong
impression while comparing layouts across ratios.

It now sits centred in a slot as tall as the tallest preview can be, which
is the 720px ceiling renderPreview already clamps to - so the slot can
never be shorter than its contents.

Verified across every ratio: heights run 711 down to 427 while the phone's
centre stays at 360px in all of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
