From db25b36dd6ab2236f14987ec85a78df29f0aa4ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:59:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 272/547] Draw the navigation as the three shapes Android
 actually uses

Square, circle, triangle rather than arrow-style icons, left to right. That
is the order Samsung ships and what most phones in the wild are set to;
stock Android and Pixel reverse it and every skin lets it be swapped, so it
is a coin toss either way - and cosmetic regardless, since the strip exists
only to make the preview read as a device.

The three are deliberately not the same size. They cannot be: a triangle in
the same bounding box as a square covers half its area and looks noticeably
smaller, and a circle inscribed in that box covers about 79% and looks
smaller again. Drawn at equal boxes the row would read as shrinking left to
right. The triangle gets the largest box and the square the smallest, which
is the same optical correction made between a square and a round letter in
a typeface.

