From bb8ce14ecad09054342b20a7af1d086a4563c89b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:09:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 277/547] Listen together: Android integration and settings
 screen

MediaPlaybackBridge is the only Android-aware piece, and stays thin - if
logic accumulates there it belongs behind the seam where it can be
tested. Speed changes leave pitch at 1 so Media3 time-stretches through
Sonic rather than resampling, which is what lets drift be corrected
without anyone hearing it. A follower looks in the local database before
YouTube, so a downloaded song starts immediately instead of adding
seconds of silence to something meant to feel simultaneous.

ListenTogetherManager runs its scope on Dispatchers.Main, and that is a
correctness requirement rather than a convention: both sessions touch
the player directly and Media3 permits that only from the main thread.
The transport already does its blocking IO on Dispatchers.IO behind a
channel, so nothing is lost.

MusicService hands over the bridge once the player exists and withdraws
it before the player is released - a session still ticking against a
released player would crash on its next poll.

The screen shows hosts, not devices. Only devices already sharing appear,
so an empty list is ambiguous between "still looking" and "nobody is
sharing" - it says both, along with the one thing the user can check.
Sync quality is words rather than milliseconds, since a raw figure
invites worry about a number nobody can act on.

Debug APK builds, all tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
