From caa742f2594daf85c2339506804c9efe7a7584e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:48:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 283/547] Listen together: surface why a session ended, and
 stop main-thread IO in the UI

The screen called deviceName() inline, which reads a system setting
through the ContentResolver - and the screen recomposes every second as
the drift figure updates, so it was main-thread IO on a one-second
timer. Resolved once instead.

The host list was remembered once rather than keyed on mode. Browsing
has to exclude this device's own advertised name, which does not exist
until hosting starts, so a flow built beforehand would offer the host
the chance to follow itself.

BYE carried a reason that never reached anyone. That was the whole point
of having one: without it a host that stopped sharing and a dropped WiFi
connection look identical from the follower's side - the session simply
vanishes and the user cannot tell which happened or whether retrying
would help. Now shown, along with the version-mismatch case that would
otherwise be the most baffling failure of all.

Remaining hardcoded English moved into string resources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
