From 8c58ca5ced5a535f6227ca55517bcce537e766d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:12:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 284/547] Fix artist pages that show the right name and none of
 the songs

YouTube spells an artist's channel id two ways: the bare UC form, and an
MPLAUC form it returns in album and playlist contexts. Every write path
normalises to the bare one before storing. Reads did not.

So arriving at an artist page from anywhere that hands over YouTube's own
id - an online album, a search result, a home row - queried the library
for a spelling no row is stored under. No artist, no songs, no albums,
while the remote fetch still resolved the name perfectly well. The
result is exactly the reported symptom: the page an artist's own songs
claim to belong to, showing their name and nothing else. Nothing errors,
because a query matching nothing is not an error.

Normalised now in all three artist-keyed view models, with the remote
fetch falling back to the raw spelling if the normalised one is refused.

That leaves a second cause with the same symptom. YouTube gives one
real-world artist more than one channel - an auto-generated "- Topic" one
alongside their real one - and the insert dedup keeps whichever id it saw
first, so every song maps to that one. Opening the page for the other
channel finds the songs filed elsewhere. The library sections now resolve
to the row that actually holds them, matched on name.

Only the library sections move, never the page itself, so this cannot
misrepresent whose page is being shown. And the query behind it returns
nothing unless the other row genuinely has songs - two artists really can
share a name - so the worst case is the page is left as it was.

Also: AlbumsDao.insert returned early when the album row already existed,
discarding the artist credits of every later, richer source. An album
first cached from a search result would keep no artist link at all. The
identical bug was already fixed for songs in DatabaseDao.insert; the
album path was missed.

