From 91731862977e35b0389646df94042e798c06e55f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:45:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 285/547] Let the patch back into the repo, and default to it

The workflow reads its patch from the repo root, so gitignoring the
patch made the file the build needs uncommittable. That guard was
protecting against a real problem - a tracked patch makes the next
format-patch embed the previous copy of itself, which doubled the
deliverable from 4.3MB to 8.7MB - but that is already prevented properly
by excluding *.patch from the generate step, so the ignore was doing
nothing except blocking the build.

build-patched-backlog.yml ("Build new APKs" in the Actions tab) now
defaults to outertune-metrolist-engine.patch, which is the patch
actually being produced. The other two keep their own defaults, and the
field is free text in every case.

