From 372d8a433d3827018a46ce7a5ffee612999cd9a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:50:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 291/547] Build workflows: expose the language filter that
 Gradle already had

app/build.gradle.kts has supported -Plocales=en,ja for a while, and its
own comment refers to "the workflow's locales input" - which was never
built. Half a feature: the machinery existed, nothing reached it.

There is now a locales input on all three workflows. Blank keeps all 50
languages, which is right for a release anyone might install; naming a
few strips the rest.

Measured rather than estimated, on a coreDebug arm64 build: 39,512,602
bytes with all languages against 37,530,159 with en,ja - 1.98MB, and 89
string configurations down to 2. The comment in build.gradle.kts guessed
1.4MB and was low.

English is added by the build whatever is asked for. It is the base
values/ resource, so dropping it would leave any string a chosen language
happens not to translate with nothing to fall back to.

The run summary now says which languages were kept, since an APK that is
suddenly 2MB smaller with no other explanation is a worrying thing to
find later.

Also reverted a wrong turn: I started adding an android:localeConfig by
hand before the build told me androidResources.generateLocaleConfig is
already true, so AGP writes that file itself and the Android 13 per-app
language picker has always worked.

