From 6619337bcb66f7920ee36796ae2c4acfc2ef9714 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:24:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 294/547] Prefer the artist channel that lists the actual song

The previous version asked whether a channel lists any songs at all,
which is a guess at whether it is the right channel. The question
actually being asked when someone taps "view artist" on a track is
whether that channel has *that track* - and the two differ exactly where
it matters: a channel can carry a full Songs shelf of other material
while the song in hand sits on a different channel of the same name.

The song id now travels with the navigation, as an optional argument, so
callers that have no particular song - an album, a search result - are
unaffected and fall back to the weaker test.

Matched anywhere on the page rather than only in the Songs shelf, since a
track can legitimately be listed under Singles and a channel that has it
at all is the one worth showing. If none of the candidates lists it, the
original stands: a page with something on it beats no page.

The picker passes it too. Choosing from that list picks a name, not a
channel, so the same ambiguity applies to an explicit choice.

Also: desktop/SIGN-IN.md, which is groundwork rather than code. The whole
problem is getting a music.youtube.com cookie into the app, and the four
ways of doing that differ by two orders of magnitude in cost - an OAuth
redirect does not yield one at all, and an embedded browser is ~150MB
against a 47MB jar, which would undo the reason this port has no native
dependencies. Written down so tomorrow starts from the decision rather
than from the survey.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
