From 8c0cdae85f83bd1ca27457fb869eb62289948220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:33:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 304/547] desktop: put the action buttons where the Android
 player puts them

The like and equaliser buttons were below the transport row, first left
aligned and then - after a wrong reading of Player.kt - centred under it.
Both were wrong. Player.kt's infoBlock draws ActionButtons inside the
title row, to the right of a weighted title/artist column, so they land
against the right edge on the same line as the song's name. They act on
the song, not on playback, which is why they sit with the song's name
rather than with the controls.

They are also filled discs rather than bare glyphs: 36dp of the primary
colour holding a 24dp onPrimary icon, 7dp apart. The fill matters over
album art, where a tinted glyph competes with whatever is behind it.

The queue handle follows the same source: a centred chevron above the
queue's name, not a left-aligned chevron beside "Up next". That needed a
title on QueueState, threaded from the four places a queue is started.

The chevron is a single mark, not Material's double one - the double
reads as "jump to the end" and this sheet opens in stages. Scaled about
its centre onto the grid centre, because the stock 480x296 glyph at
y=564 reads small and low when it is alone on its line. The geometry
test caught both the size and the offset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
