From 32469254dd6667bdac1d2382d520cd9308276c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:01:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 308/547] desktop: pin down which artist a click actually opens

Extracted the offset mapping out of the composable and tested it. Worth
doing on its own because getting it wrong is invisible in the running
app - every name renders, every underline appears, and clicking one just
opens a different artist, which is precisely the failure clickable
credits were added to fix.

Fixed one real disagreement while extracting it: the separator was
counted on "the cursor has moved" while the string builder counted it on
"index > 0". Those agree for every ordinary credit list and diverge the
moment a name is empty, leaving every range after it two characters
adrift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
