From 1d58c197675b637f05fc3db3ca15bda4cab46ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:46:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 310/547] desktop: fix the player's proportions, dials, queue
 and clickable credits

Most of this is correcting things that were wrong rather than missing.

**Sizing.** The player looked broken at every window size and the reason
was density. Android runs at 2x or 3x, so a 72dp play button is a couple
of hundred physical pixels and the cover beside it is about five times
that. A desktop window runs at 1x: the cover, being a fraction of the
window, grew to nine hundred pixels while the button stayed at
seventy-two. Same numbers, and a play button that had become a speck
against a wall of album art. Everything now scales with the window and
the cover is capped, so the ratio matches the phone at any size.

**Dials.** Ported RotaryDial properly. The first attempt drew an arc and
a pointer line, which is exactly what that file's own comment warns
against - it read as a slider bent into a circle. The dark disc, the
bezel and the pointer on the face are the component, not decoration.

**Colour.** Dials, band sliders and the seek bar all take their colour
from where their value sits: yellow low, green middle, blue high. The
response graph uses the same three colours by height rather than by
frequency, so a boost is blue wherever in the spectrum it happens to be.
Note this is the reverse of the app's own valueGradientColor, which runs
blue-to-yellow; the desktop follows the direction that was asked for.

**Compressor.** Two rows of knobs spread evenly, as the mobile panel
does it, and shown only while it is on. Five knobs in one left-aligned
row read as a strip bolted on beside the heading.

**Queue.** Two states instead of three - the middle "peek" step meant
closing it took two clicks. Flicking up now opens it over the whole
window, sliding, and clicking the bar toggles.

**Equaliser.** Scrolling up over the player opens the drawer, which is
what "scroll up to see it" was supposed to mean; the handle could only
be clicked before.

**Credits.** Rebuilt as one composable per name rather than one string
with click offsets mapped back to ranges. The offset version passed its
test and did not work in the app, and even when it works it fails
silently - two characters out and clicking one artist opens another.
Unlinked credits are now clickable too, which is the actual bug: on any
song whose artists came back without channel ids, nothing on the line
responded at all. The underline still marks the ones with a real
channel. The pointer becomes a hand over each name.

Play/pause is a rounded square while playing and a circle while paused.
The spectrum bars are off - between the credits and the seek bar they
read as something the player was doing rather than the song. The
overflow menu is there as a plain dropdown, with only the items the
desktop can actually perform: absent callbacks mean absent items, so
nothing in it promises a feature that has not been written.

