From 2e5579140563dcbfcdbbf007dc3f6760be2c5c58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:57:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 318/547] desktop: the home feed, so signing in finally buys
 something

Four working sign-in routes had been feeding nothing at all - the
account was authenticated and then the session sat unused, which is the
largest single gap this build had against the phone.

It needed no new networking. YouTube.home() is already in the shared
:innertube module and already reads YouTube.cookie, which the desktop
sets at startup, so a personalised feed only needed somewhere to put it.

Sections are handed back as the module models them rather than flattened
into a local type: they carry four kinds of item and the screen treats
each differently, so converting them here would mean reconstructing the
distinction on the other side. Songs play with the rest of their row
behind them; albums and playlists are both a playlist id underneath, so
they play without needing an album page to open first; artists open
their page. Anything else - a video, a podcast episode - has nowhere to
go here and is filtered out rather than drawn as a card that does
nothing when clicked.

Empty says which kind of empty it is. "Sign in to see recommendations"
and "YouTube has nothing for this account yet" need different things
from the reader: one is a button, the other is a shrug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
