From 89200547a426ad290a20b64f98ff71c39d8132e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:09:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 319/547] desktop: sweep - four real problems from reading back
 what I wrote

A comment claimed the theme animated between tracks and nothing did it.
That is worse than not having animated it, because a reader trusts the
comment over the code. The reasoning was sound - a cover's colours land
a moment after the song, so a hard switch flashes the wrong scheme then
the right one - so the animation now exists rather than the claim being
deleted. Only the roles that carry colour are eased; animating forty
fields to move six is per-frame work for nothing.

Scroll-to-close on the equaliser could never have worked and was written
as though it did. Once open the panel is its own full-window overlay, so
the handler underneath never sees another scroll. Removed, with a note
saying why, since it looks like an omission otherwise.

The home page split the window half and half between the feed and the
library, and the split did not move when one side was empty. They are
one scrolling column now, with liked and recently played as rows above
the recommendations - they are the two lists looked for by name rather
than browsed to.

A fourth download-index read was still on the main thread; the other
three were moved when the freeze was fixed and this one was missed.

Also: a feed that failed once stayed failed until restart, so there is a
retry; and the three compiler warnings in this module are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
