From 2f36006306e9148f494da39163409c02211e1df6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:13:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 320/547] desktop: album pages

Unblocks "View album" in the player menu, which existed as a callback
with nowhere to go, and gives the home feed's album cards somewhere to
land other than straight into playback.

One request answers the whole screen: YouTube.album() returns the
metadata and the tracks together, keyed by browse id, which is what
every link into an album already carries - a song's album.id, a feed
card's browseId.

The header is wide rather than stacked. A phone puts the cover above the
title because it has no width to spare; copying that here would leave
two thirds of the row empty beside a square.

Track numbers rather than thumbnails in the list, since every song on an
album shares the album's cover - a column of forty identical thumbnails
carries nothing and takes the width the titles want.

Shuffle hands the queue a shuffled list rather than turning shuffle mode
on. "Shuffle this album" is a way of starting it, not a setting that
should still be in force for whatever gets played next.

"View album" only appears when the song actually carries one. A menu
entry that opens an empty page is worse than one that is absent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
