From b5ee673cc4038b288ea1558214bc42b979474915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:13:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 322/547] desktop: fix settings throwing on open

AccountPane kept its own verticalScroll when it was moved into the
settings page, which scrolls too. A scrollable nested in another
scrollable on the same axis is measured with an unbounded maximum
height, and Compose refuses that outright - so settings did not merely
look wrong, it threw as soon as it was opened.

The commit that moved it said "unchanged, just relocated". That was the
mistake: unchanged was not safe. It was its own screen when it had its
own scroll, and a section does not scroll itself.

Its "Account" heading went too, since the section it now lives in
already provides one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
