From 7771b6df30c6c3fed90457d101d10a212903749d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:44:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 325/547] Fetch streams without the session, so signing in
 stops breaking playback

Signing in made every stream source fail with "Sign in to confirm you're
not a bot" - the account that was meant to improve things was what
stopped the music.

The cookie is correctly gated on the client supporting login, so the
no-auth clients were never the problem. IOS is loginSupported, so once a
cookie existed the player request became authenticated, and YouTube
expects a proof-of-origin token from an authenticated device client. This
build has no way to produce one, so it was refused.

Streaming needs no session at all. Browsing still authenticates - that is
what the home feed and the library are for - and only the stream fetch
goes out anonymously.

YouTube.player gains an `authenticated` flag defaulting to true, and
InnerTube.player a cookie override defaulting to the shared one, so every
existing caller including the whole Android app behaves exactly as
before. Only the desktop passes false.

If this reappears, the real answer is the proof-of-origin token itself
rather than another client in the list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
