From 40168b73deac91a73ff68b1ff327fe9b233b1688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:32:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 329/547] desktop: saved playlists, and scrolling past the
 equaliser closes it

Two things asked for, neither large.

Playlists saved on YouTube now appear beside the local ones, under their
own heading, rather than on a tab of their own - they are the same kind
of thing to whoever is looking for them, and a tab means knowing which
of two places a playlist lives in before being able to find it. They
play rather than open, since there is no page for an online playlist
yet, and a card that opens nothing is worse than one that does the
obvious thing with what it holds.

completed() follows the continuations, because a library is exactly
where the first page is not the answer - anyone with more than a couple
of dozen would silently lose the rest.

One bug found while adding it: the pane returned early on "no local
playlists", so with saved ones present and none made here it would have
shown "No playlists yet" over a list that was not empty.

Scrolling past the bottom of the equaliser now returns to the player -
the gesture that opened it, reversed. Accumulated rather than acted on
at once: a scroll that merely *ends* at the bottom would otherwise
dismiss the panel the moment it arrived, so reaching the last band would
close the thing being reached for. A deliberate push past the end is a
different motion from landing on it, and the threshold is what tells
them apart.

