From 914ae2e696d07e20d5420c70111140c2e827bf32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:07:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 331/547] Discord presence: fit every string to what Discord
 actually accepts

Discord validates activity strings and rejects the *whole* presence when
one is out of range - it does not trim, and it does not report. So a
track titled "4" is below the two-character minimum and one carrying
three features and a remix credit is over the hundred-and-twenty-eight
limit, and both produced no card at all. That reads as rich presence
being broken rather than as one title being unusual, which is why it is
worth fixing even though most songs were fine.

A song with no credits sent a blank state and failed the same way; it
now falls back.

Short titles are padded rather than replaced - a song really is called
"4", and showing its name with an invisible space after it is truer than
substituting something else. Long ones are cut at a word boundary when
one is near the end, and never between the halves of a surrogate pair:
anything outside the basic plane is two UTF-16 units, and a cut between
them leaves a lone surrogate, which is not a character and is rejected
outright. That would have hit only the few titles ending in an emoji,
which is exactly the kind of bug that never shows up while testing.

Twelve tests, including a property check that every awkward input lands
inside the accepted range.

Also finished a comment in DownloadUtil that trailed off mid-sentence
where an argument had been removed.

