From e5dc9c1010e153ece3faa418264ec03878133b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:12:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 334/547] Downloads: fix a scan race and a leftover
 poisoned-state gap

scanDownloads() and the init-triggered rescanDownloads() shared one
plain busy flag with an early-return guard, so a scan landing while the
other was still running silently skipped instead of running - the
auto-scan on app start could end up doing nothing. Replaced the flag
with a real Mutex so the second caller waits its turn instead of being
dropped.

Separately, only downloadedSongs() excluded the STATE_INVALID sentinel
rows from an earlier version of the download-state fix. Every other
"is this downloaded" query - the Downloaded Songs sort orders, and the
download counts in Albums/Artists/Playlists - still counted a poisoned
row as a real download until the next scan healed it. Made them all
consistent.
