From 552f12f4ded98f64d1cae29cab896789f2161c35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:44:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 335/547] desktop: Discord rich presence

Ports :kizzy as-is rather than reimplementing it - the module is plain
kotlin("jvm") on ktor with no Android dependency, so it is the same
gateway client the phone uses, not a lookalike. RpcText comes along
duplicated for the same reason Biquad and Compressor already are: a
pure Kotlin file with nothing to gain from porting piecemeal.

Settings gets a token-paste flow (manual entry only for now - the
phone's WebView token capture has no desktop equivalent yet), a test
connection button, and the enable switch. Presence updates are driven
by song-id and play/pause changes only, not by positionMs ticking every
frame, matching MusicService's single-writer pattern on Android.

Brought HANDOVER.md and PARITY.md up to date while in there - both had
drifted well behind the home feed, downloads, albums, lyrics and
settings work already shipped, still listing them as the biggest gaps.
