From 1840c34e39bc98f1c831a6de74bbcda26128e401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:25:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 336/547] desktop: Listen Together

Ports the phone's sync protocol wholesale rather than reimplementing
it - Protocol, ClockSync, PositionAnchor, DriftCorrector, PlaybackBridge,
HostSession and FollowerSession move over byte-for-byte, package line
changed and nothing else, because none of it ever depended on Android.
A phone and this desktop build can now host or follow each other
directly: same wire format, same NTP-style clock offset estimate, same
hold/nudge/seek drift ladder.

Two pieces needed real adaptation. LanDiscovery is rewritten against
jmDNS instead of NsdManager, browsing and advertising the same
_outertune._tcp.local. service either way. DesktopPlaybackBridge
implements the PlaybackBridge seam against DesktopPlayer/PlayerQueue
instead of Media3 - TimeStretch's WSOLA stretch gives the desktop the
same pitch-preserving tempo nudge the drift corrector depends on.

Surfaced a real bug in DesktopPlayer along the way: a seek requested
before the first frame decodes (sampleRate still 0) was cleared and
discarded rather than retried, so starting a track already partway
through - exactly what joining a session mid-song needs - silently
landed at 0 instead. Fixed by only clearing the pending seek once it
is actually applied; play() and PlayerQueue.play() both gained an
optional startAtMs for it.

UI folded into the existing settings page as another section, styled
like the Discord one added earlier this session - hosting, browsing,
following, and the timing-offset dial, all state-driven off
ListenTogetherManager the same way the phone's screen drives its
manager.

61 tests carried over from the Android suite (Protocol, ClockSync,
PositionAnchor, DriftCorrector, SyncMath, LanTransport, plus the
HostSession/FollowerSession integration suite) with nothing but a
package line touched - same behaviour, same suite, both platforms.
