From ed141086947bb81d7e3a97e8c2cc826635e75876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:57:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 337/547] desktop: icons on every settings row, matching the
 phone's

Every row SettingsPane.kt and AccountPane.kt already had gets the
same icon Android shows beside it - Account, Discord, Listen
Together, Playback, Lyrics, Appearance and Library all now read like
rows on both platforms rather than a plain list on one of them.

OuterTuneIcons gained a "Settings rows" section for this, sourced
from Google's published Material Symbols Outlined set (matching the
family every existing icon here already is, confirmed by diffing
several against the app's own res/drawable vectors) rather than
guessed at. Two exceptions, each documented at the icon: ColorLens
has no Material Symbols equivalent (Symbols folded it into Palette,
which a different row already uses) and comes from the legacy
Material Icons Round set instead, scaled to this file's 960
convention; Discord's own mark is reproduced at its native 127x96
viewport rather than force-fit onto the shared grid.

No new settings were added - a row for a feature the desktop doesn't
have yet (audio quality, crossfade, sync conflict resolution, proxy)
would be a setting that does nothing, which is worse than not having
it. PARITY.md says which those are and why.

The icon geometry tests needed two adjustments once real content
existed to check: "key" is 920 units wide by design (Material
Symbols' own glyph, not a mistake), and "wifi"/"networkCheck" are
concentric arcs that genuinely touch both edges - both now documented
exceptions rather than silently loosened bounds.
