From 407f3bdb7daba667fab2468cfd8996e820ef806d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:53:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 340/547] desktop: stop paying for a prefetch that missed

Two gaps in the prefetch added a moment ago, both found by walking the
teardown paths rather than by anything failing.

A prediction that turns out wrong - the user jumps to another track
instead of letting this one run on - was dereferenced but not
cancelled, so it carried on downloading a song nobody would hear,
competing for the connection with the one they had just asked for.

Emptying the queue by removing its last entry stopped the player but
left the fetched bytes held, for a queue that no longer exists.
