Subject: [PATCH 343/547] Listen Together: fix what the sweep found

A review of the last two commits turned up six real defects in them,
one of which made the headline fix do nothing on half the platforms.

**The desktop never stored the HostListener**, so the socket-release
fix was Android-only. The field was declared and stop() called close()
on it, but startHosting never assigned it - my mirror script replaced
the `val links =` line and did not add the line after it. Start
sharing, Stop, Start on the desktop reproduced the original bug
exactly. Now tested rather than trusted: four tests cover closing a
listener, and the port-reuse one fails without the fix, which is how I
confirmed they are worth having. They bind a fixed port on purpose -
port 0 cannot tell a released port from one that was never held.

**join() had lost its finally.** Moving the cleanup after the try meant
a session that threw - Media3 refusing a call against a released
player, most plausibly - skipped it, stranding the manager in
FOLLOWING with a dangling session and letting the exception reach the
default handler. The whole loop is now wrapped, cleanup runs on every
exit, and a throw reports instead of crashing.

**A flapping host defeated the give-up timer.** The budget reset on
every successful TCP connect, so a host that accepts and then says
nothing - an orphaned listener, say - reset the clock each attempt and
retried forever. It now resets only after a session that completed a
handshake.

**"45 seconds" was 45 seconds of sleep**, counting only the backoffs
and not the connect timeouts between them, so the real wait was nearer
ninety. Measured against the clock now.

**targetPositionMs could start a song at another song's playhead.**
Ticks carry a position but no song id, so a host skipping during a load
left the finished load reading the new track's position. It now checks
the tick still describes the track it is loading, and clamps to the
duration.

**The host-browsing fix was never ported to desktop** either - same
defect, same reasoning, jmDNS instead of NsdManager.

Also: the catch around playTrack swallowed CancellationException, since
Kotlin's is an IllegalStateException.
