From f362c8e79ea3557164f0e6aea616fe323e09cf45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: notK50BML <sjiaiclubtwo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:29:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 349/547] Desktop: the equaliser now survives the window
 closing

It had no persistence at all. Closing the window discarded the switch, the
curve, and any AutoEQ correction that had been fetched - which is minutes of
searching for one specific pair of headphones, and the one curve nobody could
rebuild by ear.

Saved profiles on top of that, as on the phone: every preset name doubles as a
profile, Save writes an override that wins over the built-in curve from then on,
"Revert to saved" and "Revert to default" are the two different undos, and a
typed name makes a profile that has no factory curve at all. Nudging a band
deliberately keeps the chip selected rather than deselecting it - that is what
leaves Save something to act on.

Curves are stored as bands, not as twelve gains. An AutoEQ correction arrives
with its own frequencies, its own Q per band and a shelf at each end, and
storing gains alone would quietly apply someone's correction to the wrong
frequencies while still looking like a curve.

The compressor is persisted beside it, since the two are lost together, but
deliberately not folded into a profile the way the phone does: there the two
share a card, here the compressor is its own section with its own meter, and a
tone chip silently changing how hard the track is compressed would be a surprise
from a control that appears to be about tone. Tempo and pitch stay unpersisted
on purpose - restoring 0.8x on launch would read as a broken player.

Two things that would have been per-frame SQLite writes on the Compose thread:
band drags persist on release, and the compressor's knobs - which have no
end-of-gesture callback - persist 400ms after they settle.

A malformed curve reads as nothing rather than as a broken filter. setPeaking
divides by Q and by the sample rate, so a zero or a NaN out of a corrupt file is
not a wrong-sounding curve, it is silence or noise, surfacing long after the
write that caused it. Compressor dials are left alone by contrast - it coerces
every one into range itself, so refusing the snapshot would throw away five good
dials over one bad one.

15 tests over the codec, written on the awkward shapes: shelves, non-integer Qs,
and profile names containing the tab and newline the format uses as separators.
