From 239c1bf91d241c680e8a1547cc2907ec1a42e560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: notK50BML <sjiaiclubtwo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:19:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 353/547] Audio upscaling: the DSP core, as a harmonic exciter
 rather than DSRE

DSRE is the wrong engine for a player, for two reasons that are not matters of
taste.

It is written offline. filtfilt is zero-phase, which means non-causal - forwards
over the whole array, then backwards over the whole array - and scipy.hilbert is
an FFT over the whole file. Neither exists for something that has the next 20ms.

And frequency shifting is not pitch scaling. Partials at 4, 8 and 12kHz shifted
up by 6kHz land at 10, 14 and 18kHz, which is no longer a harmonic series of
anything; the ear hears inharmonic content above a note as a separate metallic
artefact rather than as the note being brighter. Generating harmonics keeps the
relationship - 9kHz produces 18kHz, the octave above - and that is what "the
same instrument with its air back" consists of.

So this is a harmonic exciter, the approach Calf's and ffmpeg's aexciter take.
Per-sample, allocation-free, no transform.

The band planning is the part specific to this problem, and aliasing decides it.
A waveshaper generates harmonics above Nyquist too, and those fold back down as
inharmonic noise across the whole spectrum - which sounds like static and is
worse than doing nothing. So the input band is [cutoff/2, sampleRate/4]: the
lower edge puts the second harmonic of the lowest excited content exactly at the
cutoff, and the upper edge puts the second harmonic of the highest excited
content exactly at Nyquist. Nothing the second harmonic makes can fold, which is
what makes this safe at 44.1kHz with no oversampling. The drive is fixed rather
than tied to the amount control, so turning it up cannot walk the shaper into
the region where the third and fifth harmonics - the ones that do fold -
dominate.

Lossless and Opus are refused outright, as is any format not recognised:
guessing a cutoff wrong means generating harmonics into a band that already has
music in it, which is damage rather than a missed opportunity.

Eleven tests, measuring the spectrum rather than listening to it - content
checked where it belongs, then checked for absence in the two places folding
would put it. Verified load-bearing by widening the input band, which fails
them.

Not yet wired to the player or to a setting.
---
