From 7f5ae6f20fb554e15c7616df65ca403ada2dfb80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: notK50BML <sjiaiclubtwo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:56:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 361/547] Fix the docked transport riding up, and give the
 headroom a control

**The bar moved because the scroll area was allowed to shrink.** It had
weight(1f, false) - fill = false - so the scrolling column took only as much
height as its content needed, and the transport bar below it sat wherever that
left it. With the equaliser panel now collapsing when switched off, both panels
off made the content short enough for the bar to slide up the screen. It is a
docked bar; it does not move.

**And the equaliser only appearing to cut is arithmetic, not a bug - but it
needed a control.** Measured, a +12dB band holds that band where it was and
drops everything else by 12dB:

    band   pre-gain   net @1kHz   net @100Hz
     -12      0.0       -12.0        -0.2
       0      0.0         0.0         0.0
     +12    -12.0        +0.0       -11.8

Boosting cannot make a full-scale signal louder - there is nowhere above full
scale to go - so the equaliser turns everything else down to make room, and
raising a slider is heard as the rest of the track getting quieter. That is what
stopped the distortion, and it is also surprising enough to want a say in, so
Settings > Equalizer now has Automatic (as now, never distorts), Half, and None.
Default unchanged.

**One set of transport sizes.** The equaliser's row ran 34/38/44 and the queue
drawer's ran 32/32/36, so the same five controls were visibly different sizes
depending on which sheet was open. Both now use TransportSize, which keeps the
three tiers - play/pause is the one being aimed at in a hurry, skip is used
often, shuffle and repeat are set once and left - rather than flattening them.

Known failure, pre-existing and unrelated: SessionTest's handshake test times
out under full-suite load. It scopes onto Dispatchers.IO, which is a JVM-wide
64-thread pool shared with LanTransportTest's real sockets; when those hold
threads this test's coroutines are never scheduled. It passes alone.
