Subject: [PATCH 364/547] Home refresh: stop making nine network calls in a
 queue

A refresh took about ten seconds because load() ran every request in order and
none of them needed to be: the liked playlists, then three artist pages one
after another, then two songs each needing a next() before its related(), then
home, then explore, then the recent-activity sync. Nine or more round trips end
to end, so the wait was all of them added together.

They run together now, so it takes as long as the slowest one. The only
sequencing left is the one that is real - a song's related() needs the endpoint
its next() returns - and even there the two songs no longer wait for each other.

Each branch catches its own failures, which matters more here than it looks: a
failing async cancels its parent scope and takes its siblings with it, so one
provider being down would have emptied the whole screen rather than leaving a
gap where its own section goes.
