From c70a53b0ea0a81363dadf856d3083090767ac04c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:53:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 366/547] Replace the waveshaper with a look-ahead limiter; let
 the EQ drawer follow the finger

- PeakLimiter: 1.5ms look-ahead, linked-stereo gain limiter in place of the
  tanh soft-clip that distorted every boost on Half/None headroom (measured
  30dB+ less third harmonic).
- Global EQ writes settle like per-song ones, so the service's DataStore
  collector stops dragging the audio back behind the slider mid-drag.
- Pending EQ writes are flushed when the panel closes instead of being lost.
- Response curve scale locked to the faders' range.
- The pull-down handle drives the panel's sheet directly with a velocity
  fling, the same way the queue drawer works; the sheet is now the single
  source of truth for whether the panel is open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
