From f1e6f7aa1400b8815c0cc690058a25692f98536d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:09:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 367/547] Desktop: fix the blank full player, match the Android
 EQ and queue

- The cover background was an unweighted Row child, so it took the whole
  width and the player and docked queue rendered at zero width. It now
  sits behind everything; the player has its own Box, the queue docks
  beside it, and the equaliser covers the whole window.
- Equaliser reordered into Android's three cards: Equaliser (title,
  reset, switch; presets, faders, response curve), Compressor, and
  Additional settings (tone/playback dials, AutoEQ, save). Sections fold
  away when switched off; headings share titleLarge.
- Faders fill from 0dB with a 0dB tick instead of from the bottom; bass,
  balance and treble dials are centred.
- Queue header shows title, position and total length; the playing row
  is highlighted with a now-playing badge.
- Player colours come from the cover at the background's brightness, so
  buttons stay visible in a light window. Artist links underline on hover.
- Offscreen UI snapshot harness (OT_SNAPSHOTS=dir) for checking layouts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
