From 6841ad288d88b7b0037ee68a6f0df9b888391c11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:23:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 368/547] Desktop: navigation rail, search pill and mini player
 like the phone

- Main window gets Android's landscape navigation: a NavigationRail with
  Home, Songs and Playlists centred and Settings at the foot, replacing the
  "Settings"/"Playlists" text buttons. Choosing a section leaves any open
  artist, album, playlist or search.
- Search is a filled pill with a magnifier and a clear button; clearing it
  leaves the search.
- Mini player shares the rail's surface colour, uses a rounded 48dp cover
  and a filled play button that shows play when idle.
- Settings drops its back button now the rail does that job.
- Snapshot harness renders the whole window from a throwaway library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
