From 9897701e8c73bfbe7f47b3b51296adb93da0d5bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:03:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 370/547] Open YouTube playlists on desktop; stop bass boosts
 distorting

- Desktop: saved YouTube playlists and Home playlist cards open a page
  (cover, Play, Shuffle, every song via continuations) instead of trying
  to play blind and silently doing nothing.
- Desktop EQ had no headroom: a boost on a full-scale track was clipped
  flat at the output. It now pre-attenuates by the curve's peak (the
  phone's Automatic headroom) and ends in the look-ahead limiter.
- Limiter (both apps): 5ms look-ahead and a 60ms hold before release.
  With a 60ms release alone the gain rose and fell on every cycle of a
  bass note - amplitude modulation heard as gritty distortion on bass
  boosts. The window maximum is a monotonic queue so the longer window
  costs nothing extra per sample.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
