From 97a0fdc7ef60eafa77428d67beeec0dde70962e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:04:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 375/547] Android: choose and order the player's title-row
 buttons

- Any of the menu's actions (like, download, sleep timer, equaliser, lyrics, radio, add to queue/playlist/library, artist, album, share, details, tempo and pitch) or the menu itself can be a button, up to five, in any order. Settings > Player > Player buttons: the Tab arrangement dialog plus a live preview row and left-to-right position numbers; a warning when the menu is turned off; Reset gives Like + menu.
- Every action now lives once, in PlayerActions, used by both the menu and the buttons.
- Replaces the 'show equaliser button' and 'show sleep timer on player' switches; their values seed the new setting so nothing changes on update. Custom player layouts follow it for sleep and equaliser.

