From df9c4390b5871d0d647a4820e50bcf03b92177a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:29:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 379/547] Desktop: Library with YouTube sync; font picker and
 freeze fixes

- Library section (was Songs): Songs from Liked / History / Downloaded with sort, filter, play and shuffle; Artists from your listening plus your YouTube library; Albums saved on YouTube.
- Sync with the signed-in account on sign-in and on demand: liked songs merged in YouTube's order (nothing unliked), saved albums and library artists. Likes and unlikes made here are sent to YouTube.
- Font list read from Skia off the UI thread; AWT's font enumeration loaded every font on the UI thread and froze the window.
- Settings are saved on a background writer, flushed on close.
- The app-wide song actions are built once; a new copy every recomposition redrew the whole window.
- FreezeWatchdog writes every thread's stack beside the library if the UI thread stalls for 2s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
