From 1d29f82194ebd4eb61543f2e3cd8c705331784f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:55:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 385/547] Desktop: modern Windows file picker and local music
 folders

- FilePicker: the modern Explorer-style picker (IFileOpenDialog via a small C# shim PowerShell compiles once into the data folder, warmed up at startup), with folder picking and multi-select; falls back to the Java dialogs. Used for adding music folders, backups and cookies.txt.
- Settings > Local music: add folders (several at once), remove, rescan; a scan also runs at start. Songs appear under Library > On this computer and their artists under Artists.
- Tags via jaudiotagger: title, every artist (multi-value ARTISTS, else ARTIST split on ; / feat. ft. but not & or ,), album, length. Cover art from the file or a cover/folder image beside it. Lyrics from an .lrc beside the file or embedded, else online.
- Playback: the decode loop now takes any PcmSource; YouTube AAC and local files share EQ, compressor, tempo, visualiser and balance. MP3, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, WAV and AIFF through Java Sound plugins (fat jar now merges their service files); M4A through the app's own AAC path (M4aReader), since the AAC plugin misread ordinary M4A.
- Local songs are ordinary library songs (local_file table, schema 8): likeable, playlist-able, counted in Stats.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
