From cb32e3242efa6a94c9bfe48a0e20fe0044dda361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:01:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 386/547] Android: Smart headroom

A fourth headroom setting (Settings > Equalizer > Headroom > Smart): instead of turning every track down by the whole boost, it tracks how close the music actually comes to full scale and takes off only the part of the boost that would not fit - easing down in 0.1s, back up over about a second, starting each track and seek fully protected, with the limiter for anything sudden. Equaliser Studio uses it too. AUTO, HALF and OFF are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
