From 2cd133d5643b597e4b7aa364d92b81caa6e0d3b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:31:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 388/547] Desktop: Windows media controls

Hooks into System Media Transport Controls through JNA and the raw WinRT ABI (combase RoGetActivationFactory -> ISystemMediaTransportControlsInterop::GetForWindow, then vtable calls; ids and slot orders from the Windows SDK IDL, the ButtonPressed handler id derived with WinRT's pinterface algorithm). Media keys work while the window is unfocused; the volume flyout, quick settings and lock screen show title, artist and cover with play/pause, next and previous. All calls run on one MTA thread; the window's own media-key handling stands down while this is active, and everything stays off if Windows refuses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
