From 892e08b198c05237128cd3891d26b370c7867ed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:23:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 391/547] Desktop: phone settings ported - normalisation,
 persistent queue, play counting, sleep fade, region, lyrics providers, backup

- Audio normalisation from YouTube's loudness figure (turns loud tracks down only), through a new gain stage in the shared playback loop that the sleep fade also uses.
- Remember the queue: saved as it changes and every 10s, restored paused at the last position; Play resumes there.
- Skip songs that cannot play (after 1.5s, if there is a next).
- Count a play after N% of the song (default 30%) instead of at its start.
- Sleep timer: fade out over the last 30s; a default time offered first.
- Content language and country for YouTube (Home, search, charts).
- LRCLIB and KuGou can each be turned off.
- Back up library to a .backup zip (VACUUM INTO) and restore one at the next start, keeping the replaced library as library-before-restore.db; phone backups still merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
