From eb1b0acf16834339f7ac392b3aaa5178704aa1ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:16:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 392/547] Desktop: playing bars, hideable side queue, animated
 shuffle, player race fix

- Recompose only what shows the playback position (window no longer redraws per tick)
- Animated now-playing bars over the current song's cover everywhere it is listed,
  plus a highlight on the playing row
- Lyrics close and menu buttons moved to the bottom right, lifted off the edge
- Side queue can be hidden (button on the player bar), follows the current song
- Shuffle icon morphs between straight and crossed arrows, as on the phone
- Fix a stale decode job closing the next song's audio line / overwriting its state,
  which left the player stuck on one song
- Dials: shift + wheel coarse steps now work (Windows sends it as a sideways scroll)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
