From e04be6fb45b93c54b2bee426a33004b77322ec70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:28:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 400/547] Android: link local artists to YouTube Music

After each local scan, LocalArtistLinker matches local files' artists to their YouTube Music
channel under ArtistCreditEnricher's rule (exact name, a channel with a picture, the artist's own
over a Topic one) and moves their songs onto it - artist page, picture and library then treat them
as one artist. Names already in the library as a real artist link offline; names with no artist
are remembered for a month, names unlinked by hand for good. Local titles with "feat." are
enriched too.

Artist menu: "Link to YouTube Music" for a local artist (search and pick), "Unlink local files"
for a linked one. Settings > Local media: "Match local artists on YouTube Music" (on by default).

