From db7285b8da46b29606477e8001ce8c4de3a3bfc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:35:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 401/547] Listen Together: faster reaction, wider offset, no
 stutter from drift correction

- The host sends a change (play/pause, seek, skip, speed) the moment it sees it, polling every
  100 ms, instead of at the next once-a-second tick - up to a second less lag on every action
- Timing offset range +/-3000 ms on both apps (was +/-500), for Bluetooth speakers and TVs
- Drift correction resamples instead of time-stretching. On desktop the stretch buffered and
  dropped audio each time a correction started or stopped - a gap every few seconds - and on both
  it spliced the sound continuously while any correction was applied, heard as distortion.
  Largest correction 2% (was 5%)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../listentogether/DriftCorrector.kt          |  4 +-
 .../outertune/listentogether/HostSession.kt   | 39 +++++++++++++++--
 .../listentogether/MediaPlaybackBridge.kt     | 10 +++--
 .../settings/ListenTogetherSettings.kt        | 10 +++--
 .../desktop/DesktopPlaybackBridge.kt          | 10 ++---
 .../dd3boh/outertune/desktop/DesktopPlayer.kt |  4 +-
 .../outertune/desktop/DriftCorrector.kt       |  4 +-
 .../dd3boh/outertune/desktop/HostSession.kt   | 39 +++++++++++++++--
 .../dd3boh/outertune/desktop/SettingsPane.kt  |  4 +-
 .../dd3boh/outertune/desktop/TimeStretch.kt   | 42 ++++++++++++++++++-
 10 files changed, 136 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

