From e3ad51a5d6122fd18cf7cf7ebdc861731cc8c809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 405/547] Desktop: a real Windows frame without the title bar

The window keeps its native frame - shadow, rounded corners, resizing from every edge, Aero snap
when dragged, the minimise/maximise animations, maximising to the work area - with only the
caption taken away, by answering WM_NCCALCSIZE and WM_NCHITTEST through a JNA window-procedure
hook. The strip along the top is Windows' caption (drag, double-click), and the app's maximise
button is reported as the maximise button, so Windows 11's snap layouts appear on hover. Falls
back to the borderless window if the hook cannot be installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
