From 9aceaa1e3785da5f1462b3e30f3434db41b07d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:30:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 412/547] Layout editor for Windows; the desktop player follows
 imported layouts

Editor (tools/layout-editor.html):
- A Phone / Windows switch. Windows previews a landscape window drawn as the desktop player draws
  itself - its caption buttons, close button and queue bar - with every block at the desktop's real
  sizes for that window, measured against the same player area the app uses. Window shapes to
  check against (16:10, 16:9, 3:2, 21:9) and Windows presets, starting from the player as it ships.
- Every icon is now exactly what the apps draw: the remaining approximations (seek, sleep timer,
  equaliser, menu) replaced by the Material Rounded paths the apps use.
- Files say which player they are for ("platform"); each app refuses the other's, since the same
  percentages describe a tall phone and a wide window completely differently.

Desktop:
- Settings > Player and audio > Player layout: open the editor (bundled, opens on Windows), import
  its file, reset to the built-in player. Travels in settings profiles (Player).
- An imported layout places every block - cover (or lyrics), title, progress, each transport and
  action button, the queue handle - at its centre and width as a percentage of the player area.
  The editor's default, imported, lands on the built-in player.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
