Subject: [PATCH 415/547] Layout editor in the Android app; one Player buttons
 block; revert to the original layout

- Android: Settings > Appearance > Player layout > Open the layout editor - the same editor,
  bundled as an asset and shown in-app. It starts from the layout in use, and Apply puts a new one
  on the player directly (validated as an imported file is); no download/import round trip.
- "Revert to the original layout" in both apps and in the editor itself.
- The editor's four fixed action buttons (sleep, like, equaliser, menu) are now one Player buttons
  block - the buttons chosen in Settings, previewed with the default like and menu. As on the
  phone's player, it sits beside the title: in the stacked preview always, and free placement
  starts it there. Older files' separate buttons fold into it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
