From 9e2b15d054d82e3bc2a41feaafc68f64c585c747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:52:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 422/547] Make the layout editor's phone preview match the real
 player exactly

The editor now draws the phone from a dp model of Player.kt, checked on a 1080x2400/420dpi
emulator: the guided default and the free layout seeded from it land within 1px of the built-in
player, and the app draws imported layouts where the editor shows them.

- Editor: "Stacked" is "Guided"; the default preset is the built-in player (no spacing, 32dp
  inset); free placement is seeded from the guided rects; a density field; placeholders are
  like, download, equaliser and the menu.
- Android: imported guided layouts honour side padding, cover size, radius and hiding; free
  blocks are centred and take no inset; the separated transport row keeps play's 8dp gaps; the
  progress block no longer overlaps its times; title alignment is honoured; a debug-only adb
  extra sets a layout for checking.
- "Add to queue"/"Play next" is no longer offered beside the player's menu, on either app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
