From a004b71b08a2cdbd038b01e18d916e5088225753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:12:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 432/547] Keyboard shortcuts: say what a reassignment cost, and
 stop reset colliding

Three problems, all of them silent.

Binding a key already in use took it off whatever had it and said nothing. That
is the right thing to do - it is the only way to reassign a key - but the first
sign of it was a shortcut that had stopped working, days later, with nothing on
screen connecting the two. bind() and reset() now report what they displaced and
the settings screen shows it, with an Undo.

Worse was the case where the key taken was the only one an action had: that
action was left bound to nothing at all, which the screen draws exactly like one
nobody has touched. Called out on its own now - "Like now has no key".

And reset() could produce a collision that bind() has always prevented. Rebind
Like off L, give L to Shuffle - allowed, because Like no longer holds it - then
reset Like, and both hold L. Dropping the override was all reset did, so it
never looked at what the restored defaults were about to land on. actionFor()
takes the first match, which is declaration order, so which action a press
reached came down to where the two happen to sit in the enum: Shuffle is
declared above Like, so L toggled shuffle and liking quietly stopped working.
reset() now displaces like bind() does, which also makes actionFor()'s
first-match well-defined rather than arbitrary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dd3boh/outertune/desktop/KeyBindings.kt   | 77 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../outertune/desktop/KeyboardSettings.kt     | 41 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/KeyBindings.kt b/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/KeyBindings.kt
index a25a3f414..07403812c 100644
--- a/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/KeyBindings.kt
+++ b/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/KeyBindings.kt
@@ -98,6 +98,26 @@ enum class KeyAction(val label: String, val defaults: List<Chord>) {
