From 21f79735daf1086eb32a59989ea80d391dbaf70a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:12:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 433/547] Desktop: scroll down over the player to put it away

Scrolling up has opened the equaliser since the drawer got its gesture. Down was
the other half of that axis and did nothing, so the only way to shrink the
player was F or Esc - the phone has had swipe-down for this all along.

Two guards it needs that opening did not. It does not fire while the equaliser
is open, and it spends the gesture: one flick on a trackpad is dozens of events,
all but the first arriving after the player has already gone, and the tail would
otherwise land on whatever the mini player sits over. Opening shrugs that off
because it is idempotent; closing is not. The clock is pushed forward by every
event, so nothing fires again until the wheel actually stops.

New setting, three ways. Anywhere is the default and keeps today's behaviour. By
cursor position confines each gesture to the half it pulls from - the equaliser
comes down from the top, the player goes away downward - which is offered rather
than imposed, because nothing marks where the halves meet and the same flick two
pixels apart does different things. Off is off.

Both directions still stand down when something underneath already used the
scroll, so reading the lyrics or the queue never moves the player. The equaliser
check also moved into its own branch: the handler used to give up early when
there was no equaliser at all, which would have taken shrinking with it.

