From badf9fa2675dabc9c0b1a32607eba26816254ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v <v@l>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:33:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 437/547] Layout editor: the preview sat half a bezel right of
 centre

.phone is border-box and carries an 8px bezel, so handing it the screen size
made the screen 16px smaller than the size everything inside was drawn against.
The surface was still laid out at the full width, so it started at the content
box's left edge and ran 8px past its right one. Every block then sat 8px right
of the real centre, and overflow:hidden cropped what went past - which is the
whole player visibly shifted to the right.

The Windows preview had it too, less obviously: the surface is positioned by
symmetric insets so it stayed centred, but preview-pixels-per-dp divided by a
width that included the frame, drawing every block about 4% too large and
overstating the usable area by 16px.

Both now size the frame so its content box is the screen. Measured after: the
surface matches the background exactly, and the transport row is symmetric about
the centre - 110 and 59 preview px either side, where it was 8px out before.

The dp model is untouched, so the 1px agreement with the built-in player that
the preview was calibrated against still holds. It was never the model that was
wrong, only what it was being drawn into.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/layout-editor.html | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/layout-editor.html b/tools/layout-editor.html
index 69bbec0af..5365f3555 100644
--- a/tools/layout-editor.html
+++ b/tools/layout-editor.html
@@ -992,6 +992,25 @@ function renderNav(heightPx, boxW) {
   }
 }
 
+/*
+ * The frame's bezel, matching the 8px border .phone carries in the stylesheet.
+ *
+ * It has to be known here because .phone is border-box: handing it the screen size made the screen
+ * 16px smaller than the size everything inside was drawn against. The surface is laid out at the
+ * full width, so it began at the content box's left edge and ran 8px past its right one - putting
+ * every block half a bezel right of centre, with overflow:hidden quietly cropping what went past.
+ * On the phone preview that is the whole player sitting visibly off to the right; on the Windows
+ * one it also made the preview-pixels-per-dp scale about 2% too large, since it divided by a width
+ * that included the frame.
+ */
+const PHONE_BEZEL = 8;
+
+/** Sizes the frame so that its *content* box - the screen - is exactly w by h. */
+function setPhoneScreen(phone, w, h) {
+  phone.style.width = (w + PHONE_BEZEL * 2) + "px";
+  phone.style.height = (h + PHONE_BEZEL * 2) + "px";
+}
+
