From e2330df0b58adfc84117007c4a9158df70b2b540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v <v@l>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:18:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 441/547] Artist credits: stop the repairs being undone, and
 merge duplicates at runtime
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The logic was mostly right. What was wrong is that its results did not survive,
which is why it read as working sometimes and not others.

insertOrHealArtist overwrote a stored artist name with any incoming one that
differed. Every ordinary write reaches it - a library sync, an album page, a
playlist load, a song being queued - and each carries whatever name its own
sparse source happened to hold, which for a renamed channel is routinely the old
one. So the artist page would repair "(G)I-DLE" to "i-dle" and the next sync put
it straight back. It now only heals a name that is provably worse: blank, or
still carrying the raw "- Topic" suffix. A song credit is not authority on what
an artist is currently called; update(artist, artistPage) still is, and is left
free to write anything.

The general duplicate merge existed only as MIGRATION_24_25 - it ran once, on
one upgrade, and never again, so every duplicate created afterwards was
permanent. There is a runtime sweep now, deliberately narrower than that
migration: it folds a locally-minted placeholder into the real channel of the
same name and refuses to touch two real channels, because a dozen bands are
called Nirvana and collapsing them is a worse fault than leaving them apart.

repointDeadTopicChannel is gated on the artist having no picture, and on the
common path - where the credit was already correct - it returned having written
none, so the gate never closed and the same search ran on every play of every
song by that artist, forever. The persist was insert(), which is IGNORE on
conflict, so even a successful lookup threw the picture away. Both fixed;
insertOrFillThumbnail only ever fills a blank and never touches a name.

relinkAll ran on lifecycleScope. MainActivity declares no configChanges, so a
rotation or a theme change destroyed the activity and cancelled the sweep
wherever it had reached - most of why the repair appeared to work only
sometimes. It is process-scoped now, guarded against overlapping runs, and
catches per song so one unreadable row no longer abandons every song after it.

The remote-artist sync was writing titles raw, putting "- Topic" names back into
the table the migrations existed to clean, and reading with the raw id while
inserting the normalised one - so an MPLAUC… artist never received its bookmark,
picture or name on any sync. And enrichment now runs once after the whole sync
rather than inside the library-songs leg alone: liked songs, albums, artists,
playlists and recent activity all wrote credits and were never looked at.

Featured-artist parsing missed "featuring" entirely - feat\.? matches the first
four letters and then demands whitespace - and took only the first clause, so
"A ft. B (ft. C)" lost C. It now takes every clause and accepts w/ as well.
Deliberately still not "with", "x" or "vs": those are ordinary words in titles
far more often than they introduce a credit, and each false positive costs a
search and can add a wrong artist to a song.

artistByNameIgnoreCase was LIMIT 1 with no ORDER BY. With duplicates present it
returned whichever row SQLite reached first, so new credits scattered across
both and the pair fed itself - neither ever became the one everything pointed
at. Ordered now: a real channel first, then one that has a picture, then by id
so the answer is at least repeatable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
