From 988ecf25afcd6c02d0f9005472c23ad7a39507e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:50:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 443/547] Desktop: choose which artist to open when a song
 credits several
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Go to artist" opened whoever happened to be credited first, everywhere - the
song panel, the player's menu and the player's artist button - so on a feature
or a duet the second artist could only be reached by searching for them.

With more than one credit, those now ask which. In the song and player menus
the panel itself turns into the list - "Go to artist" slides it over to the
artists and "← Back" slides it back - rather than stacking a second popup on
the first. The player's artist button opens the same list on its own.

The rows are the phone's ArtistDialog: the artist's picture in a circle (or
their initial until the library has cached one), the name in bold. Unlike the
phone nothing is dimmed: a credit with no channel still opens the unlinked
page that lists your files by that name and offers to link it, so it is only
marked "Not linked to YouTube", never refused.

A song with one credit is unchanged - the tile still goes straight there.

MenuPanel gains a page slot (shown in place of the tiles, sliding in and out)
and MenuTile a keepOpen flag for tiles that lead into a page. creditedArtists()
is shared by every caller and drops an artist credited twice, so a feature
that is also the main artist does not make a one-artist song ask "which?".
Unit-tested, and rendered through the real click flow in UiSnapshots.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
