From 5f97b89b9acecaae432bba64c4480d426e22552a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:27:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 448/547] Artist credits: names kept current everywhere,
 (G)I-DLE parsed whole, and an off switch

- ArtistNameRefresher: any artist whose song is shown in a list is queued and checked in the
  background. A real channel's page is fetched and its current name written, so "(G)I-DLE" becomes
  "i-dle" everywhere without anyone opening the artist; a channel id YouTube now redirects has its
  credits moved to the channel it redirects to; a placeholder credit is searched and folded into
  the channel it names; and the duplicate sweep runs after each batch. One request at a time, 1.5s
  apart, each artist at most once a week (remembered across launches), so it cannot draw YouTube's
  automated-query throttle.
- The feat. clause is read by a small scanner instead of a pattern, so a name with brackets of its
  own is kept whole - "(feat. (G)I-DLE)" - while "ft. B (ft. C)" and "ft. A [Deluxe]" still stop at
  the bracket; a spaced dash ends an unbracketed clause ("ft. B - Remix").
- Settings > Library and content > Artist credit enrichment, on by default. Off, none of it runs:
  no sweep, no per-song enrichment, no refresh.
- mergeArtistInto() is the one place a duplicate is folded away, shared by the sweep and the
  refresher.

