From a54cf45f3ca8fae09e1f92b63e895a2979dc9c1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:28:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 449/547] Player: stop a finished song replaying once by itself

Two paths replayed audio nobody asked for.

- Swipe to skip (on by default): on a track change the cover grid is scrolled to the new song,
  starting from the previous song's cover. That scroll counts as "in progress", so the swipe
  handler read it as a swipe back and called seekToPreviousMediaItem() - the song that had just
  ended played again from the start, once, untouched. A programmatic scroll is now never a skip.
  Portrait and landscape both.
- A failure to load the next song is reported only once the current one has been read to the
  end, while the player still names the current song. The retry blamed that song, dropped its
  good URL and re-prepared it at its position, so its ending replayed up to twice. Within the last
  three seconds with a next song waiting, the next song is now the one retried, from its start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
