From 19c9a7ac7e0f625375f4bebc71477099a4d28658 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:31:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 450/547] Desktop player: the bar and button right from the
 first open, and seeks that land where dropped

- Opened on a queue restored from last time, the full player showed pause and no seek bar:
  nothing was loaded, so the player reported no duration, and the button only offered "play"
  while Paused, not Idle. Pressing it started the song while it went on saying pause. The button
  now offers play whenever nothing is playing or loading, and until the song starts the bar uses
  its known length and the restored position; seeking there moves where it will start.
- Dragging the bar while paused snapped it back to where it had been, and the song only jumped
  when resumed: the seek waited for the decode loop, which was held. The held loop now lets a
  seek through, applies it, and goes back to waiting.
- Seeking while playing flicked the bar back to the old position for a moment, because the loop
  wrote its position over the pending seek. seekTo() shows the target at once, and the loop
  leaves the readout alone until the seek is applied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
