From 537d2a3e6b4edf5c5c45a581252b43ca9285f13f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:36:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 451/547] Shuffle: one animated icon on both apps, from
 parallel arrows to the phone's crossed shuffle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The desktop drew its own curved arrows and the phone swapped between two unrelated drawables, so
the two players' shuffle buttons looked nothing alike. Both now draw the same icon: off is the
phone's two parallel arrows, on is its Material shuffle, and between them the arrows swing across
each other while each head turns with its line - the corner heads of the on glyph are the off
chevrons laid along a 45° line, so it is one shape morphing rather than a cross-fade. The arrow
that passes underneath opens a gap where they cross, as the Material glyph has.

Android's player, queue and equaliser-panel buttons use it (ShuffleButton); the notification keeps
the static drawables, which are the same two end states.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
