From ae69c01ed7bb7ad2c83ddaf7432e8330faf6583c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:40:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 452/547] Desktop: a Visualiser switch that does something, "no
 player buttons" that stays empty, and a menu that cannot eat clicks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Settings > Appearance > Visualiser did nothing: the spectrum bars were taken out of the player in
  an earlier redesign and the setting and its plumbing were left behind. Turned on, the bars are
  drawn above the seek bar again, in the built-in layout and in custom ones.
- Turning every player button off stored "", which is also what an untouched setting reads as, so
  it came back as the legacy row - sleep, like, download, equaliser, menu. "None" is stored as its
  own value now (PlayerButtonKind.NONE). PlayerButtonsStorageTest.
- The ⋮ panel is a focusable popup: while it exists, every click outside it goes to closing it. A
  panel on its way out is no longer focusable, and it is removed shortly after closing even if its
  closing animation never reports back, so it can never sit invisibly over the app swallowing
  every click.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
