Subject: [PATCH 455/547] Desktop queue: drag near the edge scrolls, and the
 row you grab is the row that moves

- Holding a row near the top or bottom of the full player's queue scrolls it, faster the nearer the
  edge, as on the phone; the held row stays under the pointer and keeps stepping past the songs
  going by.
- Grabbing a row could drag a different song. The handle's gesture is keyed by the song and
  outlives reorders, but it used the position the row had when it was first drawn - so after any
  move it dragged whatever now sat at that old place. It reads the current position now. Same fix
  in the playlist editor.
- Moving the top row scrolled the list after it (a lazy list keeps its first visible row in view
  by key), so the rows jumped out from under the pointer. The scroll position is pinned across
  each step.

