From 70f09456e3941abc1a122397ec0ac38a5230df2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:59:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 456/547] Desktop: clicks in the full player work again

The wrapper that keeps the full player's clicks from reaching the page beneath consumed every
pointer event - after the player's own controls had seen it. A click is cancelled when a later
handler consumes the pointer moving while it is held, so any click whose pointer drifted a pixel
between press and release did nothing: the button lit up and the song did not pause, the queue did
not open. A hit node with pointer input already hides the siblings beneath it, so the wrapper now
only listens. Broken since the player became an overlay (680d94970).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
