From 8a2bf981024d86276cc1c22152133cff836d3b0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:13:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 460/547] Desktop: the phone's Account and sync options, each
 doing what it does there

Settings > Account and sync had the sign-in and nothing else. Now, signed in:
- Use login for browsing content (YouTube.useLoginForBrowse).
- Show / copy login token, for signing in elsewhere.
- Automatically sync - on sign-in and at start - and Sync now, with its result.
- What to sync, in the phone's letters: liked songs, library songs (liked videos and uploads, a
  new "YouTube library" source in Songs), albums, artists, playlists (Home's and the Library's
  "Your YouTube playlists" now come from the sync) and recent activity (a Recent activity row
  first on Home). Unticked, a kind is not fetched and not shown.
- Sync mode: read only stops likes made here being sent to YouTube.
- Conflict resolution: overwrite also unlikes local songs the account no longer has liked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
