- Spellings: the sweep grouped by exact name, so "i-dle", "I-DLE" and "idle" never met. It
  groups by artistKey now - lower case, no Topic suffix, letters and digits only - and still only
  folds placeholders into the one real channel they match, never one real channel into another.
- Topic channels: YouTube's auto-generated "i-dle - Topic" is a channel of its own, and with the
  suffix stripped it sat beside the real one as a second real channel the sweep rightly would not
  merge on a name. The refresher now recognises a Topic page by its raw title and folds it into the
  channel its songs credit, when two or more agree.
- Only what was on screen got checked, so an old name elsewhere stayed. At start every non-local
  artist is queued - placeholders first, then names shared by several rows - for the same gentle
  weekly check, so renames and merges apply across the library without anyone browsing to them.

