From a2f772170cf5fa0e1975cea97e1aa7d7f474d8ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:54:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 472/547] Desktop lyrics: a skip or a dropped connection no
 longer means "no lyrics" forever

The providers catch everything, cancellation included, so a song skipped while its lyrics were
being looked up - or any lookup made offline - came back as nothing and was cached as "this song
has no lyrics", with no expiry: that song showed "No lyrics found" from then on.
- Nothing is cached once the lookup has been cancelled.
- "None" is recorded only when every enabled provider answered, not when one failed.
- A recorded miss is asked again after a week.
Also: the loading spinner is reset however a lookup ends (a cancelled one left it turning), and the
artist sent to the providers has no " - Topic" suffix, as on the phone.

