From e1b37c0f7ada427a2acf8fca07b730a9054b1531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:04:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 486/547] Unlike safety net: closes the gaps that could still
 lose or reverse a change

Audited end to end on both platforms; what was found and fixed:
- A sync in the minute before a change reached YouTube Music undid it: YouTube's list did not have
  it yet, so a song just unliked came back and one just liked was removed. The liked-songs sync now
  leaves a song alone while its change is waiting (LikeSync / LikePushes .isPending).
- A failed send was dropped silently - likeVideo returns its failure as a Result, which the
  runCatching around it never saw - and the next sync then reverted the change. Failures are seen
  now and retried twice (after 5s and 30s); a newer change for the song supersedes a retry.
- Android: songs the sync unliked to match YouTube raised the undo bar, whose Undo would have liked
  them again on the account. Only unlikes the user made are offered.
- Android: a song whose bar had timed out was counted again by the next unlike's bar, and that
  Undo liked it again too. Each bar forgets its songs when it goes.
- Android: a local file's like is no longer sent to YouTube.
- Windows: the undo bar sat under the full player, which covers the window - so an unlike with the
  full player's heart, the likeliest slip, never showed Undo. It shows over the player now.

Covered by LikeSyncTest (13) and LikePushesTest (5), which run the real objects with the wait
shortened and the sender recorded: undo restores the liked date; an unlike taken back sends
nothing; several changes send only the last; leaving or closing sends what waits; a failed send
is retried; a sync-made unlike is not offered; a timed-out bar does not come back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
