From 317c4ca01235266dede7fe91ecbd2d923f408934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:34:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 487/547] Desktop local files: 24-bit FLAC plays, and the seek
 bar is there before play

A 24-bit FLAC did not play at all: the FLAC decoder only produces PCM at the file's own depth, and
asked for 16-bit it refused ("Unsupported conversion"), so the song failed the moment it started -
title up, no seek bar, a play button that did nothing. Such a file is decoded at its own depth now
and each sample narrowed to 16 bits on the way out. Checked against a real 24-bit FLAC: it plays,
reports its length at once, and pauses and resumes.

A queue restored onto a local song also showed no seek bar until play was pressed: songs from the
library carry no length, and the fallback only knew YouTube's. A file on this computer's own
length is used.

