From 2b485d0d5e0f9bc3103ec9bd8e8969d910a33128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:39:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 488/547] Desktop local files: their own player buttons, Remove
 from library, in Downloaded songs

Files on this computer were offered everything a YouTube song is: like, download, copy link, start
radio, view album - none of which can mean anything for a file already here.
- They never show those now: not in the player's buttons, its menu, the mini player, a song's
  menu or a row's quick buttons.
- The player has a separate set of buttons for them, on by default, which out of the box is just
  the equaliser beside the menu (Settings > Player: Separate buttons for local files).
- A song's menu offers Remove from library: the file stays where it is, and later scans pass it
  by until it is restored under Settings > Local media > Removed from library. Removing rather
  than deleting, because deleting someone's music file from a music player's menu is too easy to
  regret, and a plain removal would have come back with the next scan.
- Downloaded songs lists music on this computer too, after the downloads.

