From 449c72cda2f496d22352f1be058e8f0c3f5c981d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:59:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 494/547] Stats from other devices: no double counting, and
 only the period shown

Plays read from the account's YouTube Music history (Settings: include plays from other devices)
were added on top of local plays. But a device that shares its plays with YouTube Music has those
plays in the history too, so every one of them counted twice. A song now counts the larger of its
local and history plays: never double, and a song played only elsewhere still shows its plays.

The history was also added whole to every period, so a week's chart gained plays from months ago.
History has no timestamps, only sections (Today, Yesterday, This week, Last week, then months);
each is now dated by the oldest a play in it could be, and only sections inside the period count.
A section that cannot be dated counts for all time only.

The totals above the chart include what the history adds, so they agree with it.

Shared by both apps in innertube (HistoryTally); the desktop's Stats follow next.

