From cd3b5789d64f3ce89f8d96ed57a70fed18e40d10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:37:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 503/547] Android unlike safety net: likes really do wait a
 minute now

The re-check found the delay was being defeated. Every like button - the song menu's heart, the
YouTube song menu's, multi-select Like all / Remove like, and the player's and notification's like
- called toggleLike(), which schedules the change to reach YouTube Music a minute later (and not
at all if undone), and then also syncUtils.likeSong(), which sent the same change straight away. So
an accidental unlike reached the account at once, before Undo could stop it: Undo put the song
back here, but YouTube's own list had already moved.

