From 8d68d4110d4dfccb2ee4fd8e7aad93bf5726ca18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:04:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 506/547] Android: repaired artist credits everywhere a song is
 shown, under their page names

The credit enricher repairs a song's stored credits - "X & Y" split into two channels, "(feat. Z)"
credited - and the name refresher keeps each artist under its channel's current name. But only
the library's own lists showed that. Everything built from YouTube's data - home shelves and cards,
search, artist and album pages, online playlists, the YouTube song menu - and the queue and player,
which keep a snapshot from when the song was queued, showed the raw credits under whatever name
the song's data spelled them.

Every one of those now asks the same thing (shownArtists): the library's credits when it has the
song, and otherwise the song's own credits under each artist's library name by channel id - the
name its page shows. The player's artist links follow the repaired credits too.

Also:
- Inserting a song the library already has no longer adds back credits the enricher removed. An
  album page or related list re-added the raw "X & Y" or a retired alias channel beside the
  repaired ones; a song that already has credits now keeps them.
- The artist page title drops a "- Topic" suffix, as the stored name does, so the page reads the
  name the songs credit it under.

