From 8549ef314bfa3506833d4a119ce8dc4a72ffeec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:10:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 507/547] Desktop: repaired artist credits everywhere a song is
 shown, under their current names

The desktop repaired a song's credits in the library (ArtistLinks: "X & Y" split, "(feat. Z)"
credited) but showed that only in the library's own lists. Search, Home cards, album and artist
pages, the player, mini player, queue, song menus, media controls - everything built from YouTube's
data - showed the raw credits. And nothing kept an artist under its channel's current name, so a
renamed act stayed under its old name on every song from before, while its page showed the new.

Now:
- Every song shown goes through SongItem.shown: the library's credits when it has the song, and
  otherwise the song's own credits under each artist's current name. A credits index (every song's
  credits, every artist's name) is kept by the library and rebuilt whenever either changes, so a
  repair or a rename reaches every screen.
- ArtistRenamer keeps each artist under the name its channel goes by now, read whenever its page is
  fetched anyway (opened, or its picture fetched) and, for each song that plays, once a session.
  A name read from the channel is kept: a song crediting the old spelling can no longer write it
  back (schema 11, artist.nameConfirmed).
- The artist page title drops a "- Topic" suffix, as the stored name does, so it reads the name
  the songs credit it under.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
