From 77fceb42ff13cddd608024481bb5589c80e6cb23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:17:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 515/547] Desktop: volume keys stick, the app's own close
 button sends waiting likes, the library closes

From a review of the Windows app:
- The sleep timer's loop set the volume to full every second whether or not a timer was running,
  so the volume keys lasted about a second. It only touches the volume while a fade is under way
  now, and puts back the volume the fade started from.
- The app's own caption-bar close button - the usual way out on Windows - only stopped the player,
  so a like made in the last minute never reached YouTube Music. Both close paths go through one
  quit that sends them.
- The library was never closed: the last settings and the saved queue could be lost on the way out
  and SQLite was never closed cleanly. A shutdown hook closes it on every way out, the updater's too.
- The seek keys moved 10 seconds whatever "Seek by" said; they follow it now, as the buttons do.
- The media play/pause key did nothing on a queue restored from last time; it starts it now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/Main.kt      | 46 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/Main.kt b/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/Main.kt
index 6d4332ad1..727110753 100644
--- a/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/Main.kt
+++ b/desktop/src/main/kotlin/com/dd3boh/outertune/desktop/Main.kt
@@ -157,11 +157,24 @@ fun main() = application {
         settings.equalizerStore().applyTo(player.equalizer, player.compressor, player.balance)
     }
 
+    // One way out, whichever close button is used: playback stopped and likes still waiting sent.
+    // The app's own caption bar - the usual path on Windows - only stopped the player, so a like
+    // made in the last minute never reached YouTube Music.
+    val quit = {
+        player.stop()
+        LikePushes.flushBlocking()
+        exitApplication()
+    }
+    // And the library closed once the window has finished with it: the last settings and the
+    // queue written, SQLite closed cleanly - on every way out, the updater's included.
+    remember(library) {
+        Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(Thread { runCatching { library.close() } })
+    }
+
