From cf0467c44540c32f7952d233d954d3e9da6d2b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:27:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 517/547] Desktop downloads: covers kept offline, no second
 fetch, nothing on the UI thread

- Covers are kept on disk as well as in memory (one file per picture, the largest copy seen, pruned
  past 200MB), so a downloaded song has its cover offline and a start does not fetch every cover
  again; downloading a song keeps a large copy of its cover. The memory cache drops the least
  recently drawn cover rather than the oldest loaded.
- Downloading the song that is playing, or the one prefetched to play next, saves the audio already
  fetched instead of fetching it all again.
- One HTTP client for every stream fetch, so connections to the CDN are reused.
- The Downloaded songs list was read on the UI thread with one query per song, again after every
  song of a batch download; it is read in the background, in a few queries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
