From 6d961ba9d2ae829fc6239bd2b5f92ea8584e199b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:52:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 522/547] Song sync: a credit keeps its own channel id, and a
 sparse song can gain its guests

Every synced credit was looked up by name before its id was considered, so a song by one of the
several bands called Nirvana was stored under whichever Nirvana the library already knew, and the
lookup crossed local and remote artists - local files credited to channels, streamed songs to
local placeholders. The name now decides only for a credit with no id or one from a "- Topic"
channel, and only among artists of the same kind. The album page paths use the same rule.

Keeping an existing song's credits, which stops a raw "X & Y" or a retired alias channel being
re-added beside repaired ones, also meant a song first cached from a sparse source never gained
the guests a richer source names. Such a song now takes the extra real channels from a source
that agrees with every credit it already has; a source that disagrees still adds nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
