From 1201affc89a201222441e8447107ecf1a5ac478b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:52:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 523/547] Artist merges: only on evidence, and "Unlink local
 files" stays unlinked

The name refresher folded a channel into its namesake when the channel's page had no songs at
all, which is also what a real band whose songs sit on album shelves looks like, so two different
artists became one. It now merges only on positive evidence: the namesake credited on more of the
page's songs than the channel itself, or a Topic channel whose name is the namesake's. A Topic
channel whose artist is not in the library yet was merged into the most-credited channel on its
page, which could be a collaborator; that channel must now carry the Topic channel's own name. A
page refresh writes onto the row as it is now, so a bookmark toggled meanwhile is kept, and a
placeholder search that failed is retried sooner rather than counted as checked for a week.

LocalArtistLinker relinked a name the user had unlinked by hand on the very next scan, because the offline
name lookup ran before the check for that. The check comes first now, and its merges go through
the enricher's, so they share its lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
