Subject: [PATCH 524/547] Desktop artist credits: the phone's feat. rules, one
 id per channel, no duplicate names

The feat. parser read only the first clause, missed "featuring" and "w/", cut "(feat. (G)I-DLE)"
at "(G" and took "B - Remix" as a name. It is the phone's scanner now, every clause, with names
the song already credits taken out before the rest is looked up whole and only then split. A
combined "X & Y" is split only when every half is a real artist, and a name unlinked by hand is
no longer read as "not an artist" and split or dropped.

YouTube's MPLAUC spelling of a channel id was stored as given, so one channel existed under two
ids; it is normalised where credits enter (search results, phone backups, and every credit write).
A song whose credits repeated an id threw part-way through the write and was left half credited;
credits are now written once per id and per name, so a rename that leaves two channels with one
name no longer shows "i-dle, i-dle", whether or not any artist links exist. Local tags split on
"/" only with spaces around it, so "AC/DC" stays one artist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
