A window that was not maximised could sit with its top above the screen,
the strip and most of the window buttons off the edge, so it looked as if
it filled the screen with nothing to click. Windows keeps a real title bar
on screen; the frame now does the same for the app's strip, holding the
top of a window that is not maximised to the top of its work area.
Checked in the built app: pushed 20px above the screen it lands at 0, and
maximise, restore and the buttons' hit areas are unchanged.

