From 23408dd6942fd7ddf5c8a6fc5ec3ddae0c6b860b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:51:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 540/547] Android: fixes from the review of the last two days'
 work

- Saving a cover used java.nio.file, which Android 7 does not have: every
  finished download crashed there. A plain rename does the same atomically.
- A removed download kept in the song cache now records its length, so it
  counts as whole: downloading it again moves it back, and playback no
  longer runs off its end.
- Repairing a cut-off cover no longer deletes it before the new one
  arrives; a cover that cannot be fetched falls back to the online one.
- Station songs: noted as each starts, so a song cut off by picking
  another queue is judged by its own queue; still sent to YouTube's watch
  history, only left out of local plays.
- The credit enricher only moves a credit to another channel when the old
  channel's page really is gone (404, or loaded and names nobody) - not on
  throttling, server errors or a parse failure - and an offline lookup is
  tried again later instead of never.
- Stats totals read a slim per-song count instead of the full chart query,
  and wait for it rather than briefly inflating.
- Download icons no longer flicker as rows scroll in; the media retriever
  is released on failure; an unused EQ helper is gone.

