From ae2a58a26775c8d390dc6909bcd2ef46d9e638c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:51:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 542/547] Desktop: live stations play, radios keep going, and
 review fixes

Live streams - the 24/7 radio stations - were fetched whole like a song,
which for something with no end returned its newest five seconds: they
played that and went on to the next. They are now read a segment at a
time (each a few seconds of fragmented MP4, numbered in order), decoded by
one AAC decoder across them, the next fetched while one plays. Checked
with a live station through the real player: 30s and counting, silent.

Radios and stations ask for their next page as they run low (or, with
none offered, start a fresh radio from a recent song), instead of
stopping after the first fifty songs.

From the review:
- Stopping drops the last song's bytes and any pending seek, which a
  local file started next would have begun at.
- Covers kept on disk at 1080px are scaled to the size a row asks for
  instead of filling the memory budget at full size; =s sizes are read.
- The window-top guard only acts when the top is on no screen, so dragging
  between stacked monitors works; resizing from the top keeps the bottom
  put; minimised windows are left alone; the title-bar handle's top edge
  no longer starts a resize, and it stands down under the equaliser.
- Switching queues no longer feeds a radio's songs into the other queue;
  a remembered queue keeps whether it was a station.
- A lyrics parser error no longer cancels the other providers; a duplicate
  credits query is gone; settings search finds Provider selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
